window.VQ_CURRICULUM = (window.VQ_CURRICULUM || []).concat([{"id":"b2-set-01","title":"The Disappearing Scientist","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 01","level":"B2","set":1,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"forensic","meaning":"جنائي تحليلي","example":"A forensic specialist was called to examine the scene.","number":1,"id":"b2:001","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"alibi","meaning":"حجة غياب عن مسرح الحادث","example":"His assistant had an alibi.","number":2,"id":"b2:002","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"discrepancy","meaning":"تناقض في التفاصيل","example":"His assistant had an alibi, but a discrepancy in her account suggested that someone wanted to conceal part of the truth.","number":3,"id":"b2:003","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"conceal","meaning":"يخفي","example":"His assistant had an alibi, but a discrepancy in her account suggested that someone wanted to conceal part of the truth.","number":4,"id":"b2:004","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"misleading","meaning":"مضلل","example":"Yet the specialist warned that circumstantial evidence could be misleading.","number":5,"id":"b2:005","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"tamper with","meaning":"يعبث بـ","example":"An anonymous tip claimed that she had tried to tamper with the security system.","number":6,"id":"b2:006","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"motive","meaning":"دافع","example":"What motive would she have.","number":7,"id":"b2:007","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"plausible","meaning":"قابل للتصديق","example":"The accusation sounded plausible.","number":8,"id":"b2:008","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"contradict","meaning":"يناقض","example":"The footage seemed to contradict her story.","number":9,"id":"b2:009","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"hypothesis","meaning":"فرضية","example":"Their first hypothesis had depended on deliberate deception.","number":10,"id":"b2:010","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"deduction","meaning":"استنتاج","example":"A careful deduction suggested something else.","number":11,"id":"b2:011","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"reconstruct","meaning":"يعيد بناء","example":"To establish a timeline, the team studied surveillance footage and attempted to reconstruct the suspect's whereabouts.","number":12,"id":"b2:012","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"suspect's","meaning":"مكان وجود المشتبه به","example":"To establish a timeline, the team studied surveillance footage and attempted to reconstruct the suspect's whereabouts.","number":13,"id":"b2:013","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"establish a timeline","meaning":"يحدد تسلسلا زمنيا","example":"To establish a timeline, the team studied surveillance footage and attempted to reconstruct the suspect's whereabouts.","number":14,"id":"b2:014","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"surveillance footage","meaning":"تسجيل كاميرات المراقبة","example":"To establish a timeline, the team studied surveillance footage and attempted to reconstruct the suspect's whereabouts.","number":15,"id":"b2:015","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"circumstantial","meaning":"أدلة ظرفية","example":"Yet the specialist warned that circumstantial evidence could be misleading.","number":16,"id":"b2:016","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"reveal a pattern","meaning":"يكشف نمطا","example":"That apparent coincidence helped the team reveal a pattern of technical errors.","number":17,"id":"b2:017","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"anonymous tip","meaning":"بلاغ مجهول المصدر","example":"An anonymous tip claimed that she had tried to tamper with the security system.","number":18,"id":"b2:018","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"interrogate","meaning":"يستجوب","example":"A detective wanted to interrogate the assistant immediately.","number":19,"id":"b2:019","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"deliberate deception","meaning":"تضليل متعمد","example":"Their first hypothesis had depended on deliberate deception.","number":20,"id":"b2:020","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"verify the claim","meaning":"يتحقق من الادعاء","example":"The specialist decided to verify the claim before accusing anyone.","number":21,"id":"b2:021","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"apparent coincidence","meaning":"مصادفة ظاهرية","example":"That apparent coincidence helped the team reveal a pattern of technical errors.","number":22,"id":"b2:022","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"unravel","meaning":"يفك لغزا","example":"When they finally managed to unravel the message.","number":23,"id":"b2:023","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"deceptive","meaning":"خادع","example":"One apparently deceptive message was actually a warning written in code.","number":24,"id":"b2:024","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"},{"term":"unresolved","meaning":"غير محسوم","example":"His sudden departure remained an unresolved ethical question.","number":25,"id":"b2:025","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-01"}],"story":{"title":"The Disappearing Scientist","paragraphs":["When Dr Vale disappeared from his laboratory, a forensic specialist was called to examine the scene. His assistant had an alibi, but a discrepancy in her account suggested that someone wanted to conceal part of the truth. An anonymous tip claimed that she had tried to tamper with the security system. The accusation sounded plausible, yet the specialist warned that circumstantial evidence could be misleading.","To establish a timeline, the team studied surveillance footage and attempted to reconstruct the suspect's whereabouts. A detective wanted to interrogate the assistant immediately. However, the specialist asked a different question: what motive would she have? The footage seemed to contradict her story, but its clock was running seven minutes fast. That apparent coincidence helped the team reveal a pattern of technical errors.","Their first hypothesis had depended on deliberate deception. A careful deduction suggested something else: Dr Vale had been collecting evidence of falsified scientific results. The specialist decided to verify the claim before accusing anyone. One apparently deceptive message was actually a warning written in code.","When they finally managed to unravel the message, the team found directions to a remote cabin. Dr Vale was safe, protecting documents until an independent review began. His sudden departure remained an unresolved ethical question: was hiding the truth temporarily justified in order to expose a greater wrong?"],"questions":["Why was the assistant’s alibi initially doubted?","What changed the interpretation of the surveillance footage?","What was Dr Vale trying to protect?","What ethical dilemma remains at the end?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-02","title":"The Ethical Algorithm","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 02","level":"B2","set":2,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"algorithmic bias","meaning":"تحيز الخوارزميات","example":"She suspected algorithmic bias.","number":26,"id":"b2:026","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"machine learning","meaning":"تعلم الآلة","example":"A school introduced a scholarship system based on machine learning.","number":27,"id":"b2:027","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"facial recognition","meaning":"التعرف على الوجوه","example":"The software also used facial recognition without clear consent.","number":28,"id":"b2:028","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"ethical implications","meaning":"تبعات أخلاقية","example":"Lina asked the headteacher to explain the ethical implications.","number":29,"id":"b2:029","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"autonomous","meaning":"ذاتي التشغيل","example":"Its autonomous software produced a predictive model of students' future success, using years of training data.","number":30,"id":"b2:030","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"training data","meaning":"بيانات التدريب","example":"Using years of training data.","number":31,"id":"b2:031","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"prejudice","meaning":"تحامل مسبق","example":"Old records contained prejudice.","number":32,"id":"b2:032","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"discriminate","meaning":"يميز ضد","example":"Old records contained prejudice, and the model seemed to discriminate against students whose achievements were less common.","number":33,"id":"b2:033","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"transparency","meaning":"شفافية","example":"The company promised transparency but would not reveal a flawed assumption inside its calculations.","number":34,"id":"b2:034","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"accountable","meaning":"خاضع للمساءلة","example":"Its director said the system was accountable because computers did not have emotions.","number":35,"id":"b2:035","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"unintended","meaning":"عواقب غير مقصودة","example":"She described the unintended consequences of trusting patterns without human oversight.","number":36,"id":"b2:036","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"consent","meaning":"موافقة","example":"The software also used facial recognition without clear consent.","number":37,"id":"b2:037","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"predictive model","meaning":"نموذج تنبؤي","example":"Its autonomous software produced a predictive model of students' future success, using years of training data.","number":38,"id":"b2:038","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"human oversight","meaning":"إشراف بشري","example":"She described the unintended consequences of trusting patterns without human oversight.","number":39,"id":"b2:039","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"digital rights","meaning":"حقوق رقمية","example":"That could compromise privacy and undermine digital rights.","number":40,"id":"b2:040","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"biased outcome","meaning":"نتيجة متحيزة","example":"A biased outcome is still unfair.","number":41,"id":"b2:041","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"complex decision","meaning":"قرار معقد","example":"At first, the complex decision looked efficient.","number":42,"id":"b2:042","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"flawed assumption","meaning":"افتراض معيب","example":"The company promised transparency but would not reveal a flawed assumption inside its calculations.","number":43,"id":"b2:043","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"data protection","meaning":"حماية البيانات","example":"The students proposed responsible design: better data protection, a regulatory framework and a method allowing families to challenge a decision.","number":44,"id":"b2:044","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"regulatory","meaning":"إطار تنظيمي","example":"The students proposed responsible design: better data protection, a regulatory framework and a method allowing families to challenge a decision.","number":45,"id":"b2:045","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"challenge a decision","meaning":"يطعن في قرار","example":"The students proposed responsible design: better data protection, a regulatory framework and a method allowing families to challenge a decision.","number":46,"id":"b2:046","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"ethical dilemma","meaning":"معضلة أخلاقية","example":"They argued that an ethical dilemma cannot be solved merely by increasing speed.","number":47,"id":"b2:047","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"compromise privacy","meaning":"ينتهك الخصوصية","example":"That could compromise privacy and undermine digital rights.","number":48,"id":"b2:048","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"responsible design","meaning":"تصميم مسؤول","example":"The students proposed responsible design.","number":49,"id":"b2:049","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"},{"term":"public trust","meaning":"ثقة الجمهور","example":"Public trust grew only after leaders admitted the mistake and explained how they would prevent it from happening again.","number":50,"id":"b2:050","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-02"}],"story":{"title":"The Ethical Algorithm","paragraphs":["A school introduced a scholarship system based on machine learning. Its autonomous software produced a predictive model of students' future success, using years of training data. At first, the complex decision looked efficient. Then Lina discovered that the system had rejected several excellent students who used wheelchairs.","She suspected algorithmic bias. Old records contained prejudice, and the model seemed to discriminate against students whose achievements were less common. The software also used facial recognition without clear consent. That could compromise privacy and undermine digital rights. Lina asked the headteacher to explain the ethical implications.","The company promised transparency but would not reveal a flawed assumption inside its calculations. Its director said the system was accountable because computers did not have emotions. Lina disagreed: a biased outcome is still unfair, even if no person intends it. She described the unintended consequences of trusting patterns without human oversight.","The students proposed responsible design: better data protection, a regulatory framework and a method allowing families to challenge a decision. They argued that an ethical dilemma cannot be solved merely by increasing speed. The school suspended the automatic ranking and reviewed every application fairly. Public trust grew only after leaders admitted the mistake and explained how they would prevent it from happening again."],"questions":["Why might historical training data produce unfair decisions?","What two rights did Lina say the system threatened?","Why did the director’s argument fail?","What should responsible schools learn from the case?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-03","title":"The Ocean Treaty","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 03","level":"B2","set":3,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"marine pollution","meaning":"تلوث بحري","example":"Scientists described marine pollution.","number":51,"id":"b2:051","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"microplastics","meaning":"جزيئات بلاستيكية دقيقة","example":"Microplastics and coastal erosion along the Silver Sea.","number":52,"id":"b2:052","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"coastal erosion","meaning":"تآكل السواحل","example":"Microplastics and coastal erosion along the Silver Sea.","number":53,"id":"b2:053","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"ecosystem collapse","meaning":"انهيار النظام البيئي","example":"Fish numbers had fallen so sharply that some feared ecosystem collapse.","number":54,"id":"b2:054","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"global agreement","meaning":"اتفاق عالمي","example":"One nation proposed a global agreement with a binding commitment to reduce industrial discharge.","number":55,"id":"b2:055","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"binding commitment","meaning":"التزام ملزم","example":"One nation proposed a global agreement with a binding commitment to reduce industrial discharge.","number":56,"id":"b2:056","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"enforce","meaning":"يفرض تطبيق","example":"Another said it could not enforce expensive rules immediately.","number":57,"id":"b2:057","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"enforcement","meaning":"إنفاذ","example":"A student called Amir explained that enforcement mattered.","number":58,"id":"b2:058","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"industrial discharge","meaning":"تصريف صناعي","example":"One nation proposed a global agreement with a binding commitment to reduce industrial discharge.","number":59,"id":"b2:059","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"ecosystem recovery","meaning":"تعافي النظام البيئي","example":"He presented the scientific consensus about long-term impact and asked leaders to allocate resources for ecosystem recovery.","number":60,"id":"b2:060","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"carbon footprint","meaning":"بصمة كربونية","example":"The discussion reached a negotiation deadlock when businesses raised fears about their carbon footprint and costs.","number":61,"id":"b2:061","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"international","meaning":"تعاون دولي","example":"International cooperation finally produced a compromise.","number":62,"id":"b2:062","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"vulnerable","meaning":"مجتمعات معرضة للخطر","example":"The delegates agreed that environmental degradation was already harming vulnerable communities, but they disagreed about what to do.","number":63,"id":"b2:063","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"scientific consensus","meaning":"إجماع علمي","example":"He presented the scientific consensus about long-term impact and asked leaders to allocate resources for ecosystem recovery.","number":64,"id":"b2:064","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"allocate resources","meaning":"يخصص الموارد","example":"He presented the scientific consensus about long-term impact and asked leaders to allocate resources for ecosystem recovery.","number":65,"id":"b2:065","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"monitor compliance","meaning":"يراقب الالتزام","example":"He proposed a measurable conservation target and a practical way to monitor compliance.","number":66,"id":"b2:066","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"legal obligation","meaning":"التزام قانوني","example":"Without a legal obligation.","number":67,"id":"b2:067","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"negotiation deadlock","meaning":"جمود المفاوضات","example":"The discussion reached a negotiation deadlock when businesses raised fears about their carbon footprint and costs.","number":68,"id":"b2:068","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"public pressure","meaning":"ضغط شعبي","example":"Public pressure increased.","number":69,"id":"b2:069","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"long-term impact","meaning":"أثر طويل المدى","example":"He presented the scientific consensus about long-term impact and asked leaders to allocate resources for ecosystem recovery.","number":70,"id":"b2:070","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"precautionary","meaning":"مبدأ الاحتياط","example":"Amir suggested the precautionary principle.","number":71,"id":"b2:071","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"shared responsibility","meaning":"مسؤولية مشتركة","example":"While all parties accepted shared responsibility.","number":72,"id":"b2:072","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"environmental","meaning":"تدهور بيئي","example":"The delegates agreed that environmental degradation was already harming vulnerable communities, but they disagreed about what to do.","number":73,"id":"b2:073","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"conservation target","meaning":"هدف للحفاظ على البيئة","example":"He proposed a measurable conservation target and a practical way to monitor compliance.","number":74,"id":"b2:074","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"},{"term":"decisive action","meaning":"إجراء حاسم","example":"The agreement encouraged decisive action without ignoring economic realities.","number":75,"id":"b2:075","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-03"}],"story":{"title":"The Ocean Treaty","paragraphs":["At an international youth summit, scientists described marine pollution, microplastics and coastal erosion along the Silver Sea. Fish numbers had fallen so sharply that some feared ecosystem collapse. The delegates agreed that environmental degradation was already harming vulnerable communities, but they disagreed about what to do.","One nation proposed a global agreement with a binding commitment to reduce industrial discharge. Another said it could not enforce expensive rules immediately. A student called Amir explained that enforcement mattered: without a legal obligation, promises might achieve little. He presented the scientific consensus about long-term impact and asked leaders to allocate resources for ecosystem recovery.","The discussion reached a negotiation deadlock when businesses raised fears about their carbon footprint and costs. Public pressure increased. Amir suggested the precautionary principle: when damage may be serious, waiting for perfect certainty is dangerous. He proposed a measurable conservation target and a practical way to monitor compliance.","International cooperation finally produced a compromise. Wealthier nations would help poorer regions improve treatment systems, while all parties accepted shared responsibility. The agreement encouraged decisive action without ignoring economic realities. Amir understood that policy was not simply a matter of choosing between the environment and jobs. Real progress depended on designing obligations that different communities could meet fairly."],"questions":["Why did Amir want binding commitments?","What caused the negotiation deadlock?","How did the precautionary principle influence his proposal?","How did the agreement balance different needs?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-04","title":"The Forgotten Civilization","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 04","level":"B2","set":4,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"cultural artefact","meaning":"قطعة أثرية ثقافية","example":"She checked the dating evidence, interviewed local storytellers about oral history and compared the cultural artefact with objects from an ancient trade route.","number":76,"id":"b2:076","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"translation error","meaning":"خطأ في الترجمة","example":"Hana began to decipher the inscription and noticed a translation error in a familiar phrase.","number":77,"id":"b2:077","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"decipher","meaning":"يفك رموزا","example":"Hana began to decipher the inscription and noticed a translation error in a familiar phrase.","number":78,"id":"b2:078","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"inscribed tablet","meaning":"لوح منقوش","example":"Hana found an inscribed tablet beside a burial chamber.","number":79,"id":"b2:079","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"ceremonial object","meaning":"غرض طقسي","example":"Experts believed the people who made the ceremonial object had disappeared after a war.","number":80,"id":"b2:080","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"excavation permit","meaning":"تصريح تنقيب","example":"The team had an excavation permit.","number":81,"id":"b2:081","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"dating evidence","meaning":"دليل لتحديد العمر","example":"She checked the dating evidence.","number":82,"id":"b2:082","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"historical","meaning":"تفسير تاريخي","example":"But its first historical interpretation was controversial.","number":83,"id":"b2:083","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"oral history","meaning":"تاريخ شفهي","example":"She checked the dating evidence, interviewed local storytellers about oral history and compared the cultural artefact with objects from an ancient trade route.","number":84,"id":"b2:084","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"archaeological","meaning":"سجل أثري","example":"Although the archaeological record remained incomplete.","number":85,"id":"b2:085","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"previous assumption","meaning":"افتراض سابق","example":"He argued that a previous assumption could not be overturned by one object of disputed origin.","number":86,"id":"b2:086","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"alternative","meaning":"تفسير بديل","example":"This meticulous analysis suggested an alternative explanation.","number":87,"id":"b2:087","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"ancient trade route","meaning":"طريق تجاري قديم","example":"She checked the dating evidence, interviewed local storytellers about oral history and compared the cultural artefact with objects from an ancient trade route.","number":88,"id":"b2:088","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"burial chamber","meaning":"غرفة دفن","example":"Hana found an inscribed tablet beside a burial chamber.","number":89,"id":"b2:089","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"preserve integrity","meaning":"يحافظ على سلامة الشيء","example":"The museum decided to preserve integrity by recording both interpretations in its permanent exhibition.","number":90,"id":"b2:090","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"academic dispute","meaning":"خلاف أكاديمي","example":"A senior scholar dismissed her idea, starting an academic dispute.","number":91,"id":"b2:091","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"significance","meaning":"أهمية","example":"Still, the object's significance demanded further study.","number":92,"id":"b2:092","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"disputed origin","meaning":"أصل محل خلاف","example":"He argued that a previous assumption could not be overturned by one object of disputed origin.","number":93,"id":"b2:093","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"meticulous analysis","meaning":"تحليل دقيق جدا","example":"This meticulous analysis suggested an alternative explanation.","number":94,"id":"b2:094","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"reconstruct a society","meaning":"يعيد تصور مجتمع","example":"She offered to reconstruct a society in which different communities had met for trade and ritual rather than war.","number":95,"id":"b2:095","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"ritual","meaning":"طقس","example":"She offered to reconstruct a society in which different communities had met for trade and ritual rather than war.","number":96,"id":"b2:096","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"permanent exhibition","meaning":"معرض دائم","example":"The museum decided to preserve integrity by recording both interpretations in its permanent exhibition.","number":97,"id":"b2:097","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"incomplete record","meaning":"سجل غير مكتمل","example":"An incomplete record could not explain every discovery.","number":98,"id":"b2:098","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"conclusive proof","meaning":"دليل قاطع","example":"Hana agreed that conclusive proof was lacking.","number":99,"id":"b2:099","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"},{"term":"prevailing theory","meaning":"نظرية سائدة","example":"That was the prevailing theory.","number":100,"id":"b2:100","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-04"}],"story":{"title":"The Forgotten Civilization","paragraphs":["During a university project, Hana found an inscribed tablet beside a burial chamber. The team had an excavation permit, but its first historical interpretation was controversial. Experts believed the people who made the ceremonial object had disappeared after a war. That was the prevailing theory, although the archaeological record remained incomplete. An incomplete record could not explain every discovery.","Hana began to decipher the inscription and noticed a translation error in a familiar phrase. The mark previously understood as 'battle' might mean 'journey'. She checked the dating evidence, interviewed local storytellers about oral history and compared the cultural artefact with objects from an ancient trade route. This meticulous analysis suggested an alternative explanation.","A senior scholar dismissed her idea, starting an academic dispute. He argued that a previous assumption could not be overturned by one object of disputed origin. Hana agreed that conclusive proof was lacking. Still, the object's significance demanded further study. She offered to reconstruct a society in which different communities had met for trade and ritual rather than war.","The museum decided to preserve integrity by recording both interpretations in its permanent exhibition. Visitors could see why the story remained open to debate. Hana learned that history is not a collection of perfect answers. It is a careful conversation between surviving evidence, imagination and the willingness to change one's mind."],"questions":["What caused Hana to question the prevailing theory?","Which additional sources strengthened her interpretation?","Why was the senior scholar’s objection reasonable?","Why did the museum present both interpretations?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-05","title":"The City Without Electricity","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 05","level":"B2","set":5,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"blackout","meaning":"انقطاع شامل للتيار","example":"A blackout struck Northbridge just before midnight.","number":101,"id":"b2:101","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"power grid","meaning":"شبكة الكهرباء","example":"The city's power grid had suffered from a maintenance backlog and insufficient infrastructure investment.","number":102,"id":"b2:102","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"cascading failure","meaning":"سلسلة أعطال متتابعة","example":"But engineers soon discovered an overloaded system and a cascading failure.","number":103,"id":"b2:103","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"emergency backup","meaning":"نظام احتياطي للطوارئ","example":"Hospitals could protect critical services because they had emergency backup.","number":104,"id":"b2:104","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"alternative supply","meaning":"إمداد بديل","example":"The coordination centre needed an alternative supply for essential equipment and a reliable backup for vulnerable residents.","number":105,"id":"b2:105","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"grid operator","meaning":"مشغل الشبكة","example":"At first the grid operator blamed an unexpected outage.","number":106,"id":"b2:106","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"maintenance backlog","meaning":"تراكم أعمال الصيانة","example":"The city's power grid had suffered from a maintenance backlog and insufficient infrastructure investment.","number":107,"id":"b2:107","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"infrastructure","meaning":"استثمار في البنية التحتية","example":"The city's power grid had suffered from a maintenance backlog and insufficient infrastructure investment.","number":108,"id":"b2:108","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"widespread","meaning":"تعطل واسع النطاق","example":"The widespread disruption closed shops and caused a public transport shutdown.","number":109,"id":"b2:109","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"critical services","meaning":"خدمات حيوية","example":"Hospitals could protect critical services because they had emergency backup.","number":110,"id":"b2:110","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"public transport","meaning":"توقف النقل العام","example":"The widespread disruption closed shops and caused a public transport shutdown.","number":111,"id":"b2:111","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"unexpected outage","meaning":"انقطاع غير متوقع","example":"At first the grid operator blamed an unexpected outage.","number":112,"id":"b2:112","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"overloaded system","meaning":"نظام محمل فوق طاقته","example":"At first the grid operator blamed an unexpected outage, but engineers soon discovered an overloaded system and a cascading failure.","number":113,"id":"b2:113","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"damage assessment","meaning":"تقييم الأضرار","example":"An engineer carried out a damage assessment and proposed a contingency plan.","number":114,"id":"b2:114","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"temporary generator","meaning":"مولد مؤقت","example":"Yet one temporary generator was running out of fuel.","number":115,"id":"b2:115","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"restore supply","meaning":"يعيد الإمداد","example":"Teams would restore supply in stages while monitoring the network.","number":116,"id":"b2:116","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"essential equipment","meaning":"معدات أساسية","example":"The coordination centre needed an alternative supply for essential equipment and a reliable backup for vulnerable residents.","number":117,"id":"b2:117","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"reliable backup","meaning":"بديل احتياطي موثوق","example":"The coordination centre needed an alternative supply for essential equipment and a reliable backup for vulnerable residents.","number":118,"id":"b2:118","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"prevent recurrence","meaning":"يمنع التكرار","example":"How could they prevent recurrence.","number":119,"id":"b2:119","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"coordination centre","meaning":"مركز تنسيق","example":"The coordination centre needed an alternative supply for essential equipment and a reliable backup for vulnerable residents.","number":120,"id":"b2:120","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"contingency plan","meaning":"خطة طوارئ بديلة","example":"An engineer carried out a damage assessment and proposed a contingency plan.","number":121,"id":"b2:121","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"public reassurance","meaning":"طمأنة الجمهور","example":"Officials promised public reassurance.","number":122,"id":"b2:122","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"vulnerable residents","meaning":"سكان معرضون للخطر","example":"The coordination centre needed an alternative supply for essential equipment and a reliable backup for vulnerable residents.","number":123,"id":"b2:123","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"gradual recovery","meaning":"تعاف تدريجي","example":"A volunteer group helped neighbours get medication and food during the gradual recovery.","number":124,"id":"b2:124","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"},{"term":"resilience planning","meaning":"تخطيط للقدرة على الصمود","example":"Their resilience planning required new maintenance schedules.","number":125,"id":"b2:125","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-05"}],"story":{"title":"The City Without Electricity","paragraphs":["A blackout struck Northbridge just before midnight. At first the grid operator blamed an unexpected outage, but engineers soon discovered an overloaded system and a cascading failure. The city's power grid had suffered from a maintenance backlog and insufficient infrastructure investment.","The widespread disruption closed shops and caused a public transport shutdown. Hospitals could protect critical services because they had emergency backup, yet one temporary generator was running out of fuel. The coordination centre needed an alternative supply for essential equipment and a reliable backup for vulnerable residents.","An engineer carried out a damage assessment and proposed a contingency plan. Teams would restore supply in stages while monitoring the network. Officials promised public reassurance, but many residents wanted honest answers rather than comforting words. A volunteer group helped neighbours get medication and food during the gradual recovery.","When electricity returned, leaders faced a harder decision: how could they prevent recurrence? Their resilience planning required new maintenance schedules, careful testing and money that voters might prefer to spend elsewhere. The engineer explained that a city cannot protect people merely by fixing a fault after it happens. Emergency planning and safe infrastructure are quiet investments whose true value becomes visible during a crisis."],"questions":["What deeper causes contributed to the blackout?","Why did hospitals cope better than some residents?","What made honest communication important during recovery?","What policy lesson did the engineer emphasise?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-06","title":"The Memory Experiment","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 06","level":"B2","set":6,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"cognitive bias","meaning":"تحيز إدراكي","example":"The researcher explained how cognitive bias.","number":126,"id":"b2:126","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"memory distortion","meaning":"تشوه الذاكرة","example":"Memory distortion and subconscious expectations can affect recall.","number":127,"id":"b2:127","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"recall","meaning":"يسترجع من الذاكرة","example":"Memory distortion and subconscious expectations can affect recall.","number":128,"id":"b2:128","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"long-term retention","meaning":"احتفاظ طويل الأمد","example":"Psychologist Ms Rahman invited volunteers to an experiment about short-term memory and long-term retention.","number":129,"id":"b2:129","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"short-term memory","meaning":"ذاكرة قصيرة المدى","example":"Psychologist Ms Rahman invited volunteers to an experiment about short-term memory and long-term retention.","number":130,"id":"b2:130","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"experimental","meaning":"شرط تجريبي","example":"The experimental condition seemed harmless.","number":131,"id":"b2:131","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"control group","meaning":"مجموعة ضابطة","example":"One control group watched a video of a busy street.","number":132,"id":"b2:132","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"variable","meaning":"متغير","example":"Students considered each variable.","number":133,"id":"b2:133","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"participants'","meaning":"استجابات المشاركين","example":"Yet participants' responses surprised everyone.","number":134,"id":"b2:134","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"false memory","meaning":"ذكرى زائفة","example":"Some confidently described the bicycle, creating a false memory.","number":135,"id":"b2:135","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"subconscious","meaning":"العقل الباطن","example":"Memory distortion and subconscious expectations can affect recall.","number":136,"id":"b2:136","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"attention span","meaning":"مدة التركيز","example":"From attention span to the emotional trigger in the question.","number":137,"id":"b2:137","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"misleading question","meaning":"سؤال مضلل","example":"Another group saw the same scene but received a misleading question about a red bicycle that had never appeared.","number":138,"id":"b2:138","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"reconstruct a","meaning":"يعيد تشكيل ذكرى","example":"The brain may reconstruct a memory every time someone remembers it.","number":139,"id":"b2:139","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"emotional trigger","meaning":"مثير عاطفي","example":"From attention span to the emotional trigger in the question.","number":140,"id":"b2:140","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"research ethics","meaning":"أخلاقيات البحث","example":"The class also discussed research ethics.","number":141,"id":"b2:141","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"informed consent","meaning":"موافقة مستنيرة","example":"Everyone had given informed consent.","number":142,"id":"b2:142","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"hypothesis testing","meaning":"اختبار الفرضية","example":"Their hypothesis testing suggested a measurable psychological effect.","number":143,"id":"b2:143","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"psychological effect","meaning":"أثر نفسي","example":"Their hypothesis testing suggested a measurable psychological effect.","number":144,"id":"b2:144","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"assess reliability","meaning":"يقيم الموثوقية","example":"However, Ms Rahman refused to announce a dramatic discovery before she could assess reliability.","number":145,"id":"b2:145","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"perception","meaning":"إدراك","example":"Human perception is not a perfect recording.","number":146,"id":"b2:146","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"cognitive process","meaning":"عملية إدراكية","example":"The cognitive process was complex.","number":147,"id":"b2:147","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"unexpected finding","meaning":"نتيجة غير متوقعة","example":"And a single unexpected finding could reflect chance.","number":148,"id":"b2:148","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"interpret results","meaning":"يفسر النتائج","example":"They worked to interpret results without humiliating anyone whose memory had changed.","number":149,"id":"b2:149","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"},{"term":"ethical review","meaning":"مراجعة أخلاقية","example":"Everyone had given informed consent, but the teacher's ethical review required explaining the deception afterwards.","number":150,"id":"b2:150","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-06"}],"story":{"title":"The Memory Experiment","paragraphs":["Psychologist Ms Rahman invited volunteers to an experiment about short-term memory and long-term retention. One control group watched a video of a busy street. Another group saw the same scene but received a misleading question about a red bicycle that had never appeared.","The experimental condition seemed harmless, yet participants' responses surprised everyone. Some confidently described the bicycle, creating a false memory. The researcher explained how cognitive bias, memory distortion and subconscious expectations can affect recall. Human perception is not a perfect recording: the brain may reconstruct a memory every time someone remembers it.","Students considered each variable, from attention span to the emotional trigger in the question. Their hypothesis testing suggested a measurable psychological effect. However, Ms Rahman refused to announce a dramatic discovery before she could assess reliability. The cognitive process was complex, and a single unexpected finding could reflect chance.","The class also discussed research ethics. Everyone had given informed consent, but the teacher's ethical review required explaining the deception afterwards. They worked to interpret results without humiliating anyone whose memory had changed. The experiment taught a subtle lesson: being confident about an event is not identical to being correct about it. Good reasoning begins when we test even our most convincing recollections."],"questions":["How did the misleading question influence participants?","Why did the researcher avoid a dramatic early claim?","Why was an ethical review necessary?","What lesson does the experiment teach about confidence?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-07","title":"The Whistleblower’s File","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 07","level":"B2","set":7,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"leak confidential","meaning":"يسرب وثائق سرية","example":"A newspaper received an anonymous source who offered to leak confidential documents about a factory.","number":151,"id":"b2:151","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"internal memo","meaning":"مذكرة داخلية","example":"An internal memo suggested misconduct.","number":152,"id":"b2:152","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"misconduct","meaning":"سوء سلوك مهني","example":"Yet alleged misconduct was not automatically proven.","number":153,"id":"b2:153","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"wrongdoing","meaning":"تصرف غير مشروع","example":"An internal memo suggested misconduct, but editor Maya knew that an accusation of wrongdoing could damage innocent people.","number":154,"id":"b2:154","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"anonymous source","meaning":"مصدر مجهول","example":"A newspaper received an anonymous source who offered to leak confidential documents about a factory.","number":155,"id":"b2:155","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"editorial judgement","meaning":"حكم تحريري","example":"Her editorial judgement required her to verify authenticity before publishing anything.","number":156,"id":"b2:156","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"verify authenticity","meaning":"يتحقق من الأصالة","example":"Her editorial judgement required her to verify authenticity before publishing anything.","number":157,"id":"b2:157","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"disclose information","meaning":"يفصح عن معلومات","example":"The sender agreed to disclose information only if Maya would protect identity.","number":158,"id":"b2:158","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"confidential source","meaning":"مصدر سري","example":"This confidential source feared legal exposure and might face retaliation.","number":159,"id":"b2:159","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"protect identity","meaning":"يحمي الهوية","example":"The sender agreed to disclose information only if Maya would protect identity.","number":160,"id":"b2:160","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"legal exposure","meaning":"تعرض للمساءلة القانونية","example":"This confidential source feared legal exposure and might face retaliation.","number":161,"id":"b2:161","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"professional ethics","meaning":"أخلاقيات المهنة","example":"Maya discussed professional ethics.","number":162,"id":"b2:162","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"public interest","meaning":"المصلحة العامة","example":"Public interest and editorial","number":163,"id":"b2:163","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"expose corruption","meaning":"يكشف الفساد","example":"They wanted to expose corruption.","number":164,"id":"b2:164","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"alleged misconduct","meaning":"سوء سلوك مزعوم","example":"Yet alleged misconduct was not automatically proven.","number":165,"id":"b2:165","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"investigative","meaning":"صحافة استقصائية","example":"Through investigative reporting, the journalists found credible testimony and documentary evidence.","number":166,"id":"b2:166","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"credible testimony","meaning":"شهادة جديرة بالثقة","example":"The journalists found credible testimony and documentary evidence.","number":167,"id":"b2:167","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"documentary","meaning":"أدلة وثائقية","example":"The journalists found credible testimony and documentary evidence.","number":168,"id":"b2:168","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"conflict of interest","meaning":"تضارب مصالح","example":"The records suggested a conflict of interest between inspectors and the factory owner.","number":169,"id":"b2:169","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"media scrutiny","meaning":"تدقيق إعلامي","example":"Under media scrutiny, officials first denied the findings.","number":170,"id":"b2:170","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"face retaliation","meaning":"يواجه انتقاما","example":"This confidential source feared legal exposure and might face retaliation.","number":171,"id":"b2:171","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"editorial","meaning":"استقلالية التحرير","example":"Public interest and editorial independence with her team.","number":172,"id":"b2:172","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"publish responsibly","meaning":"ينشر بمسؤولية","example":"The newsroom decided to publish responsibly.","number":173,"id":"b2:173","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"withheld details","meaning":"تفاصيل تم حجبها","example":"It included verified facts but withheld details that could identify workers who had spoken privately.","number":174,"id":"b2:174","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"},{"term":"accountability gap","meaning":"ثغرة في المساءلة","example":"Maya noticed an accountability gap.","number":175,"id":"b2:175","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-07"}],"story":{"title":"The Whistleblower’s File","paragraphs":["A newspaper received an anonymous source who offered to leak confidential documents about a factory. An internal memo suggested misconduct, but editor Maya knew that an accusation of wrongdoing could damage innocent people. Her editorial judgement required her to verify authenticity before publishing anything.","The sender agreed to disclose information only if Maya would protect identity. This confidential source feared legal exposure and might face retaliation. Maya discussed professional ethics, public interest and editorial independence with her team. They wanted to expose corruption, yet alleged misconduct was not automatically proven.","Through investigative reporting, the journalists found credible testimony and documentary evidence. The records suggested a conflict of interest between inspectors and the factory owner. Under media scrutiny, officials first denied the findings. Maya noticed an accountability gap: nobody had checked whether the public safety reports were accurate.","The newsroom decided to publish responsibly. It included verified facts but withheld details that could identify workers who had spoken privately. The final article prompted an independent inquiry and improved safety rules. Maya realised that a journalist's responsibility is not merely to reveal secrets. The harder task is to investigate carefully, protect people and explain why the truth matters without turning uncertainty into a dramatic accusation."],"questions":["Why did Maya delay publication?","How did the journalists strengthen the source’s account?","Why were some details withheld?","What balance does the story recommend for investigative journalism?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-08","title":"The Mars Colony Debate","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 08","level":"B2","set":8,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"settlement viability","meaning":"جدوى الاستيطان","example":"During a school debate about a colony on Mars, Ava defended the long-term mission while Malik questioned settlement viability.","number":176,"id":"b2:176","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"life-support system","meaning":"نظام دعم الحياة","example":"Both agreed that a sustainable habitat would need a reliable life-support system.","number":177,"id":"b2:177","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"resource scarcity","meaning":"ندرة الموارد","example":"Yet resource scarcity, radiation exposure and a powerful gravitational effect on the human body remained serious concerns.","number":178,"id":"b2:178","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"sustainable habitat","meaning":"موطن مستدام","example":"Both agreed that a sustainable habitat would need a reliable life-support system.","number":179,"id":"b2:179","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"gravitational effect","meaning":"تأثير الجاذبية","example":"Yet resource scarcity, radiation exposure and a powerful gravitational effect on the human body remained serious concerns.","number":180,"id":"b2:180","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"radiation exposure","meaning":"تعرض للإشعاع","example":"Yet resource scarcity, radiation exposure and a powerful gravitational effect on the human body remained serious concerns.","number":181,"id":"b2:181","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"psychological","meaning":"عزلة نفسية","example":"Malik raised the problem of psychological isolation and crew morale.","number":182,"id":"b2:182","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"mission objective","meaning":"هدف المهمة","example":"The space agency's mission objective was to test oxygen recycling and an autonomous rover.","number":183,"id":"b2:183","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"technological","meaning":"طفرة تقنية","example":"Engineers promised a technological breakthrough.","number":184,"id":"b2:184","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"failure probability","meaning":"احتمال الفشل","example":"Engineers promised a technological breakthrough, but scientists warned about scientific uncertainty and the failure probability of complex equipment.","number":185,"id":"b2:185","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"contingency protocol","meaning":"إجراء احتياطي","example":"The team practised remote operation during a simulated emergency and followed a contingency protocol when their systems failed.","number":186,"id":"b2:186","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"oxygen recycling","meaning":"إعادة تدوير الأكسجين","example":"The space agency's mission objective was to test oxygen recycling and an autonomous rover.","number":187,"id":"b2:187","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"crew morale","meaning":"معنويات الطاقم","example":"Malik raised the problem of psychological isolation and crew morale.","number":188,"id":"b2:188","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"ethical concerns","meaning":"مخاوف أخلاقية","example":"Ava did not ignore the ethical concerns.","number":189,"id":"b2:189","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"cost-benefit analysis","meaning":"تحليل التكلفة والمنفعة","example":"His cost-benefit analysis also asked whether the enormous budget had a viable alternative on Earth.","number":190,"id":"b2:190","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"scientific uncertainty","meaning":"عدم يقين علمي","example":"Engineers promised a technological breakthrough, but scientists warned about scientific uncertainty and the failure probability of complex equipment.","number":191,"id":"b2:191","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"viable alternative","meaning":"بديل قابل للتطبيق","example":"His cost-benefit analysis also asked whether the enormous budget had a viable alternative on Earth.","number":192,"id":"b2:192","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"long-term mission","meaning":"مهمة طويلة الأمد","example":"During a school debate about a colony on Mars, Ava defended the long-term mission while Malik questioned settlement viability.","number":193,"id":"b2:193","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"extreme conditions","meaning":"ظروف قاسية جدا","example":"Extreme conditions and limited capacity could make ordinary disagreements dangerous.","number":194,"id":"b2:194","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"limited capacity","meaning":"قدرة محدودة","example":"Extreme conditions and limited capacity could make ordinary disagreements dangerous.","number":195,"id":"b2:195","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"collective decision","meaning":"قرار جماعي","example":"She argued that every exploration involves risk, yet a collective decision should be based on evidence rather than excitement.","number":196,"id":"b2:196","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"simulated emergency","meaning":"طوارئ محاكية للواقع","example":"The team practised remote operation during a simulated emergency and followed a contingency protocol when their systems failed.","number":197,"id":"b2:197","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"autonomous rover","meaning":"عربة جوالة ذاتية القيادة","example":"The space agency's mission objective was to test oxygen recycling and an autonomous rover.","number":198,"id":"b2:198","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"remote operation","meaning":"تشغيل عن بعد","example":"The team practised remote operation during a simulated emergency and followed a contingency protocol when their systems failed.","number":199,"id":"b2:199","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"},{"term":"human survival","meaning":"بقاء البشر","example":"It was whether humans could build a safe community there without pretending that technological ambition removes human vulnerability or guarantee human survival.","number":200,"id":"b2:200","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-08"}],"story":{"title":"The Mars Colony Debate","paragraphs":["During a school debate about a colony on Mars, Ava defended the long-term mission while Malik questioned settlement viability. Both agreed that a sustainable habitat would need a reliable life-support system. Yet resource scarcity, radiation exposure and a powerful gravitational effect on the human body remained serious concerns.","The space agency's mission objective was to test oxygen recycling and an autonomous rover. Engineers promised a technological breakthrough, but scientists warned about scientific uncertainty and the failure probability of complex equipment. The team practised remote operation during a simulated emergency and followed a contingency protocol when their systems failed.","Malik raised the problem of psychological isolation and crew morale. Extreme conditions and limited capacity could make ordinary disagreements dangerous. His cost-benefit analysis also asked whether the enormous budget had a viable alternative on Earth.","Ava did not ignore the ethical concerns. She argued that every exploration involves risk, yet a collective decision should be based on evidence rather than excitement. Their teacher praised both sides: one imagined possibility, the other insisted on responsibility. The class concluded that the question was not simply whether humanity could reach Mars. It was whether humans could build a safe community there without pretending that technological ambition removes human vulnerability or guarantee human survival."],"questions":["What practical systems would a Mars colony depend on?","Why did Malik raise psychological isolation?","What different priorities did Ava and Malik represent?","What does the debate suggest about technological progress?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-09","title":"The Mountain Border Crisis","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 09","level":"B2","set":9,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"border dispute","meaning":"نزاع حدودي","example":"A border dispute forced displaced families to leave their villages.","number":201,"id":"b2:201","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"displaced families","meaning":"أسر نازحة","example":"A border dispute forced displaced families to leave their villages.","number":202,"id":"b2:202","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"humanitarian","meaning":"ممر إنساني","example":"A neutral mediator called a meeting to create a humanitarian corridor.","number":203,"id":"b2:203","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"ceasefire agreement","meaning":"اتفاق وقف إطلاق النار","example":"When a ceasefire agreement was announced.","number":204,"id":"b2:204","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"neutral mediator","meaning":"وسيط محايد","example":"A neutral mediator called a meeting to create a humanitarian corridor.","number":205,"id":"b2:205","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"escalate tensions","meaning":"يصعد التوترات","example":"A careless rumour might escalate tensions and destroy the fragile peace.","number":206,"id":"b2:206","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"diplomatic effort","meaning":"جهد دبلوماسي","example":"It took a sustained diplomatic effort to reach a settlement.","number":207,"id":"b2:207","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"impartial assessment","meaning":"تقييم محايد","example":"An international observer recommended an impartial assessment rather than another public accusation.","number":208,"id":"b2:208","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"conflicting accounts","meaning":"روايات متضاربة","example":"The two sides offered conflicting accounts of how the violence began.","number":209,"id":"b2:209","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"fragile peace","meaning":"سلام هش","example":"A careless rumour might escalate tensions and destroy the fragile peace.","number":210,"id":"b2:210","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"international","meaning":"مراقب دولي","example":"An international observer recommended an impartial assessment rather than another public accusation.","number":211,"id":"b2:211","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"provide safe passage","meaning":"يوفر مرورا آمنا","example":"Both sides would provide safe passage.","number":212,"id":"b2:212","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"cross-border aid","meaning":"مساعدات عبر الحدود","example":"Without safe passage, children and older people could not receive cross-border aid.","number":213,"id":"b2:213","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"civilian protection","meaning":"حماية المدنيين","example":"The mediator explained that civilian protection was more urgent than winning an argument at the negotiation table.","number":214,"id":"b2:214","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"political pressure","meaning":"ضغط سياسي","example":"At first, political pressure made both leaders refuse to compromise.","number":215,"id":"b2:215","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"negotiation table","meaning":"طاولة المفاوضات","example":"The mediator explained that civilian protection was more urgent than winning an argument at the negotiation table.","number":216,"id":"b2:216","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"mutually acceptable","meaning":"مقبول للطرفين","example":"The mediator proposed terms that were mutually acceptable.","number":217,"id":"b2:217","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"reach a settlement","meaning":"يتوصل إلى تسوية","example":"It took a sustained diplomatic effort to reach a settlement.","number":218,"id":"b2:218","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"enforce a ceasefire","meaning":"يفرض وقف إطلاق النار","example":"They disagreed over how to enforce a ceasefire and the number of people who could use the route.","number":219,"id":"b2:219","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"displaced population","meaning":"سكان نازحون","example":"Through confidential dialogue, the mediator proposed terms that were mutually acceptable: both sides would provide safe passage, allow independent monitors and support temporary sheltering for the displaced population.","number":220,"id":"b2:220","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"temporary sheltering","meaning":"إيواء مؤقت","example":"Through confidential dialogue, the mediator proposed terms that were mutually acceptable: both sides would provide safe passage, allow independent monitors and support temporary sheltering for the displaced population.","number":221,"id":"b2:221","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"regional stability","meaning":"استقرار إقليمي","example":"The agreement was not a lasting resolution to every historical complaint, but it helped protect regional stability and allowed humanitarian workers to act.","number":222,"id":"b2:222","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"confidential dialogue","meaning":"حوار سري","example":"Through confidential dialogue, the mediator proposed terms that were mutually acceptable: both sides would provide safe passage, allow independent monitors and support temporary sheltering for the displaced population.","number":223,"id":"b2:223","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"build confidence","meaning":"يبني الثقة","example":"Residents slowly began to build confidence in the plan.","number":224,"id":"b2:224","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"},{"term":"lasting resolution","meaning":"حل دائم","example":"The agreement was not a lasting resolution to every historical complaint.","number":225,"id":"b2:225","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-09"}],"story":{"title":"The Mountain Border Crisis","paragraphs":["A border dispute forced displaced families to leave their villages. When a ceasefire agreement was announced, a neutral mediator called a meeting to create a humanitarian corridor. Without safe passage, children and older people could not receive cross-border aid. The two sides offered conflicting accounts of how the violence began. A careless rumour might escalate tensions and destroy the fragile peace. An international observer recommended an impartial assessment rather than another public accusation.","The mediator explained that civilian protection was more urgent than winning an argument at the negotiation table. At first, political pressure made both leaders refuse to compromise. They disagreed over how to enforce a ceasefire and the number of people who could use the route. Through confidential dialogue, the mediator proposed terms that were mutually acceptable: both sides would provide safe passage, allow independent monitors and support temporary sheltering for the displaced population.","It took a sustained diplomatic effort to reach a settlement. Residents slowly began to build confidence in the plan. The agreement was not a lasting resolution to every historical complaint, but it helped protect regional stability and allowed humanitarian workers to act. A student observer learned that peace is not always a sudden moment of harmony. Sometimes it is a fragile arrangement made possible by patience, practical guarantees and a willingness to put human lives first."],"questions":["Why was a humanitarian corridor necessary?","Why were conflicting accounts dangerous?","What practical guarantees helped the sides agree?","Why is the agreement described as incomplete but valuable?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-10","title":"The Entrepreneur’s Dilemma","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 10","level":"B2","set":10,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"market saturation","meaning":"تشبع السوق","example":"But the market saturation worried investors.","number":226,"id":"b2:226","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"competitive","meaning":"ميزة تنافسية","example":"Her competitive advantage was a promise of ethical sourcing.","number":227,"id":"b2:227","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"scale up","meaning":"يوسع نطاق العمل","example":"A young entrepreneur wanted to scale up her clothing company.","number":228,"id":"b2:228","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"consumer behaviour","meaning":"سلوك المستهلك","example":"A detailed market research report suggested strong consumer behaviour trends, but a regulatory hurdle delayed the launch.","number":229,"id":"b2:229","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"profit margin","meaning":"هامش الربح","example":"That made production costs higher and reduced the profit margin.","number":230,"id":"b2:230","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"ethical sourcing","meaning":"توريد أخلاقي","example":"Her competitive advantage was a promise of ethical sourcing.","number":231,"id":"b2:231","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"production costs","meaning":"تكاليف الإنتاج","example":"That made production costs higher and reduced the profit margin.","number":232,"id":"b2:232","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"venture capital","meaning":"رأس مال مخاطر","example":"A venture capital firm offered money in exchange for a strategic partnership.","number":233,"id":"b2:233","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"strategic partnership","meaning":"شراكة استراتيجية","example":"A venture capital firm offered money in exchange for a strategic partnership.","number":234,"id":"b2:234","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"financial forecast","meaning":"توقع مالي","example":"Its financial forecast showed rapid growth if the company used cheaper suppliers.","number":235,"id":"b2:235","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"market research","meaning":"بحث سوقي","example":"A detailed market research report suggested strong consumer behaviour trends, but a regulatory hurdle delayed the launch.","number":236,"id":"b2:236","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"regulatory hurdle","meaning":"عائق تنظيمي","example":"But a regulatory hurdle delayed the launch.","number":237,"id":"b2:237","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"cash-flow crisis","meaning":"أزمة تدفق نقدي","example":"Meanwhile, a cash-flow crisis","number":238,"id":"b2:238","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"investor confidence","meaning":"ثقة المستثمرين","example":"The founder had to negotiate terms without damaging investor confidence.","number":239,"id":"b2:239","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"brand reputation","meaning":"سمعة العلامة التجارية","example":"Cutting corners could harm brand reputation and the long-term vision.","number":240,"id":"b2:240","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"sustainable growth","meaning":"نمو مستدام","example":"Nevertheless, the new plan supported sustainable growth without abandoning the company's original promise.","number":241,"id":"b2:241","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"negotiate terms","meaning":"يتفاوض على الشروط","example":"The founder had to negotiate terms without damaging investor confidence.","number":242,"id":"b2:242","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"potential downside","meaning":"جانب سلبي محتمل","example":"The potential downside of refusing the deal was serious.","number":243,"id":"b2:243","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"commercial viability","meaning":"جدوى تجارية","example":"She reconsidered the commercial viability of her business and decided to pivot strategy: instead of competing for every customer, she would focus on an emerging market willing to pay for transparent pricing.","number":244,"id":"b2:244","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"pivot strategy","meaning":"يغير استراتيجية العمل","example":"She reconsidered the commercial viability of her business and decided to pivot strategy: instead of competing for every customer, she would focus on an emerging market willing to pay for transparent pricing.","number":245,"id":"b2:245","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"emerging market","meaning":"سوق ناشئة","example":"She reconsidered the commercial viability of her business and decided to pivot strategy: instead of competing for every customer, she would focus on an emerging market willing to pay for transparent pricing.","number":246,"id":"b2:246","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"economic","meaning":"غموض اقتصادي","example":"Economic uncertainty remained, and not all stakeholder interests could be satisfied immediately.","number":247,"id":"b2:247","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"long-term vision","meaning":"رؤية بعيدة المدى","example":"Cutting corners could harm brand reputation and the long-term vision.","number":248,"id":"b2:248","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"stakeholder interests","meaning":"مصالح الأطراف المعنية","example":"And not all stakeholder interests could be satisfied immediately.","number":249,"id":"b2:249","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"},{"term":"transparent pricing","meaning":"تسعير شفاف","example":"She reconsidered the commercial viability of her business and decided to pivot strategy: instead of competing for every customer, she would focus on an emerging market willing to pay for transparent pricing.","number":250,"id":"b2:250","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-10"}],"story":{"title":"The Entrepreneur’s Dilemma","paragraphs":["A young entrepreneur wanted to scale up her clothing company, but the market saturation worried investors. Her competitive advantage was a promise of ethical sourcing. That made production costs higher and reduced the profit margin, yet customers seemed to care about fair working conditions.","A venture capital firm offered money in exchange for a strategic partnership. Its financial forecast showed rapid growth if the company used cheaper suppliers. A detailed market research report suggested strong consumer behaviour trends, but a regulatory hurdle delayed the launch. Meanwhile, a cash-flow crisis threatened the business.","The founder had to negotiate terms without damaging investor confidence. The potential downside of refusing the deal was serious. However, cutting corners could harm brand reputation and the long-term vision. She reconsidered the commercial viability of her business and decided to pivot strategy: instead of competing for every customer, she would focus on an emerging market willing to pay for transparent pricing.","Economic uncertainty remained, and not all stakeholder interests could be satisfied immediately. Nevertheless, the new plan supported sustainable growth without abandoning the company's original promise. The founder learned that good entrepreneurship is not merely about recognising demand. It is about deciding which principles must survive when money becomes scarce."],"questions":["Why was the cheaper investment deal attractive?","What risk did the founder see beyond immediate profit?","How did the business change strategy?","What broader business principle does the story defend?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-11","title":"The Digital Identity Crisis","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 11","level":"B2","set":11,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"identity theft","meaning":"سرقة الهوية","example":"When students reported identity theft after using the school portal.","number":251,"id":"b2:251","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"data breach","meaning":"اختراق بيانات","example":"The technology club examined a possible data breach.","number":252,"id":"b2:252","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"personal credentials","meaning":"بيانات اعتماد شخصية","example":"Attackers had collected personal credentials through a fake password reset page.","number":253,"id":"b2:253","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"biometric verification","meaning":"تحقق حيوي","example":"The club recommended biometric verification as an optional safeguard.","number":254,"id":"b2:254","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"password reset","meaning":"إعادة تعيين كلمة مرور","example":"Attackers had collected personal credentials through a fake password reset page.","number":255,"id":"b2:255","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"authentication","meaning":"طريقة المصادقة","example":"The original system's authentication method was weak.","number":256,"id":"b2:256","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"encryption key","meaning":"مفتاح تشفير","example":"A compromised device might have exposed an encryption key used for digital transaction records.","number":257,"id":"b2:257","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"unauthorized access","meaning":"وصول غير مصرح","example":"And a security loophole allowed unauthorized access.","number":258,"id":"b2:258","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"digital surveillance","meaning":"مراقبة رقمية","example":"The students examined digital surveillance logs and noticed cross-platform tracking that could compromise online anonymity.","number":259,"id":"b2:259","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"threat assessment","meaning":"تقييم التهديد","example":"Their teacher led a threat assessment.","number":260,"id":"b2:260","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"cybersecurity","meaning":"حادث أمن سيبراني","example":"School leaders initially wanted to hide the cybersecurity incident to avoid criticism.","number":261,"id":"b2:261","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"security loophole","meaning":"ثغرة أمنية","example":"And a security loophole allowed unauthorized access.","number":262,"id":"b2:262","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"safeguard","meaning":"يحمي المعلومات","example":"The club recommended biometric verification as an optional safeguard, not a compulsory requirement.","number":263,"id":"b2:263","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"digital transaction","meaning":"معاملة رقمية","example":"A compromised device might have exposed an encryption key used for digital transaction records.","number":264,"id":"b2:264","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"privacy breach","meaning":"انتهاك خصوصية","example":"The privacy breach was serious.","number":265,"id":"b2:265","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"compromised device","meaning":"جهاز مخترق","example":"A compromised device might have exposed an encryption key used for digital transaction records.","number":266,"id":"b2:266","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"identity verification","meaning":"التحقق من الهوية","example":"They argued that identity verification must not create fresh privacy risks.","number":267,"id":"b2:267","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"user awareness","meaning":"وعي المستخدم","example":"Other measures included user awareness sessions.","number":268,"id":"b2:268","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"trace the breach","meaning":"يتتبع الاختراق","example":"They began to trace the breach and document each technical vulnerability.","number":269,"id":"b2:269","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"technical","meaning":"ثغرة تقنية","example":"They began to trace the breach and document each technical vulnerability.","number":270,"id":"b2:270","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"online anonymity","meaning":"مجهولية الإنترنت","example":"The students examined digital surveillance logs and noticed cross-platform tracking that could compromise online anonymity.","number":271,"id":"b2:271","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"cross-platform","meaning":"تتبع عبر المنصات","example":"The students examined digital surveillance logs and noticed cross-platform tracking that could compromise online anonymity.","number":272,"id":"b2:272","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"responsible","meaning":"إفصاح مسؤول","example":"Other measures included user awareness sessions, a stronger cybersecurity policy and a clear process for responsible disclosure.","number":273,"id":"b2:273","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"cybersecurity policy","meaning":"سياسة الأمن السيبراني","example":"Other measures included user awareness sessions, a stronger cybersecurity policy and a clear process for responsible disclosure.","number":274,"id":"b2:274","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"},{"term":"digital accountability","meaning":"مساءلة رقمية","example":"The club insisted on digital accountability.","number":275,"id":"b2:275","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-11"}],"story":{"title":"The Digital Identity Crisis","paragraphs":["When students reported identity theft after using the school portal, the technology club examined a possible data breach. Attackers had collected personal credentials through a fake password reset page. The original system's authentication method was weak, and a security loophole allowed unauthorized access.","Their teacher led a threat assessment. A compromised device might have exposed an encryption key used for digital transaction records. The students examined digital surveillance logs and noticed cross-platform tracking that could compromise online anonymity. Although no banking information had been stolen, the privacy breach was serious.","The club recommended biometric verification as an optional safeguard, not a compulsory requirement. They argued that identity verification must not create fresh privacy risks. Other measures included user awareness sessions, a stronger cybersecurity policy and a clear process for responsible disclosure. Working with a specialist, they began to trace the breach and document each technical vulnerability.","School leaders initially wanted to hide the cybersecurity incident to avoid criticism. The club insisted on digital accountability: affected families needed honest information and practical steps to safeguard information. The school informed users, repaired the system and arranged an independent review. Students learned that good online security depends on both technology and the willingness to admit mistakes."],"questions":["What was the initial weakness in the portal?","Why was biometric verification optional?","Why did students oppose hiding the incident?","What is the main lesson about cybersecurity?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-12","title":"The Court of Public Opinion","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 12","level":"B2","set":12,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"media frenzy","meaning":"هوس إعلامي","example":"Within hours, social media outrage created a media frenzy.","number":276,"id":"b2:276","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"trial by media","meaning":"محاكمة إعلامية","example":"Reporter Dana worried about trial by media.","number":277,"id":"b2:277","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"public perception","meaning":"تصور الجمهور","example":"Presumed innocence and a fair hearing were essential even when public perception had already changed.","number":278,"id":"b2:278","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"sensational coverage","meaning":"تغطية مثيرة","example":"One website used a misleading headline and sensational coverage.","number":279,"id":"b2:279","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"biased reporting","meaning":"تغطية متحيزة","example":"The musician released a public statement, but biased reporting continued.","number":280,"id":"b2:280","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"presumed innocence","meaning":"افتراض البراءة","example":"Presumed innocence and a fair hearing were essential even when public perception had already changed.","number":281,"id":"b2:281","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"impartial judgement","meaning":"حكم محايد","example":"Dana knew that responsible journalism required impartial judgement.","number":282,"id":"b2:282","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"legal proceedings","meaning":"إجراءات قانونية","example":"She studied the legal proceedings and courtroom procedure.","number":283,"id":"b2:283","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"public statement","meaning":"بيان علني","example":"The musician released a public statement, but biased reporting continued.","number":284,"id":"b2:284","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"reputational damage","meaning":"ضرر بالسمعة","example":"His family considered a defamation claim because the reputational damage was severe.","number":285,"id":"b2:285","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"distorted narrative","meaning":"رواية مشوهة","example":"A widely shared fabricated quote had helped create a distorted narrative.","number":286,"id":"b2:286","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"social media outrage","meaning":"غضب وسائل التواصل","example":"Within hours, social media outrage created a media frenzy.","number":287,"id":"b2:287","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"fabricated quote","meaning":"اقتباس مختلق","example":"A widely shared fabricated quote had","number":288,"id":"b2:288","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"responsible","meaning":"صحافة مسؤولة","example":"Dana knew that responsible journalism required impartial judgement.","number":289,"id":"b2:289","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"defamation claim","meaning":"دعوى تشهير","example":"His family considered a defamation claim because the reputational damage was severe.","number":290,"id":"b2:290","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"editorial standards","meaning":"معايير التحرير","example":"Editorial standards and ethical reporting.","number":291,"id":"b2:291","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"misleading headline","meaning":"عنوان مضلل","example":"One website used a misleading headline and sensational coverage.","number":292,"id":"b2:292","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"public backlash","meaning":"رد فعل شعبي غاضب","example":"The public backlash turned against the original websites.","number":293,"id":"b2:293","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"evidence threshold","meaning":"حد الأدلة المطلوب","example":"Consulted an independent investigation and checked the evidence threshold.","number":294,"id":"b2:294","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"courtroom procedure","meaning":"إجراء قضائي","example":"She studied the legal proceedings and courtroom procedure.","number":295,"id":"b2:295","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"independent","meaning":"تحقيق مستقل","example":"Consulted an independent investigation and checked the evidence threshold.","number":296,"id":"b2:296","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"fair hearing","meaning":"جلسة استماع عادلة","example":"Presumed innocence and a fair hearing were essential even when public perception had already changed.","number":297,"id":"b2:297","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"complex allegation","meaning":"اتهام معقد","example":"A famous young musician faced a complex allegation after a video spread online.","number":298,"id":"b2:298","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"restore reputation","meaning":"يعيد السمعة","example":"Dana wrote about how a person might restore reputation after an error has spread to millions.","number":299,"id":"b2:299","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"},{"term":"ethical reporting","meaning":"تغطية أخلاقية","example":"Editorial standards and ethical reporting.","number":300,"id":"b2:300","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-12"}],"story":{"title":"The Court of Public Opinion","paragraphs":["A famous young musician faced a complex allegation after a video spread online. Within hours, social media outrage created a media frenzy. One website used a misleading headline and sensational coverage, turning an uncertain story into a public scandal.","Reporter Dana worried about trial by media. Presumed innocence and a fair hearing were essential even when public perception had already changed. She studied the legal proceedings and courtroom procedure, consulted an independent investigation and checked the evidence threshold. A widely shared fabricated quote had helped create a distorted narrative.","The musician released a public statement, but biased reporting continued. His family considered a defamation claim because the reputational damage was severe. Dana knew that responsible journalism required impartial judgement, editorial standards and ethical reporting. She refused to publish personal rumours merely because they attracted clicks.","When new evidence weakened the accusation, the public backlash turned against the original websites. Yet restoring a career was harder than correcting a headline. Dana wrote about how a person might restore reputation after an error has spread to millions. She concluded that media freedom carries an equally serious responsibility: to distinguish legitimate scrutiny from punishment without proof. The most dramatic version of a story is not necessarily the most truthful."],"questions":["What made the early online coverage misleading?","Why did Dana avoid publishing further rumours?","Why was correcting the report insufficient?","What is the difference between scrutiny and trial by media?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-13","title":"The Refugee Orchestra","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 13","level":"B2","set":13,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"humanitarian","meaning":"مساعدة إنسانية","example":"After forced displacement brought several families to a new town, volunteers offered humanitarian assistance and helped them complete an asylum application.","number":301,"id":"b2:301","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"forced displacement","meaning":"تهجير قسري","example":"After forced displacement brought several families to a new town.","number":302,"id":"b2:302","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"asylum application","meaning":"طلب لجوء","example":"After forced displacement brought several families to a new town, volunteers offered humanitarian assistance and helped them complete an asylum application.","number":303,"id":"b2:303","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"refugee status","meaning":"صفة لاجئ","example":"Some waited months for refugee status and temporary residence.","number":304,"id":"b2:304","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"integration","meaning":"برنامج اندماج","example":"Music teacher Nora proposed an integration programme built around an orchestra.","number":305,"id":"b2:305","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"language barrier","meaning":"حاجز اللغة","example":"But a language barrier made everyday communication difficult.","number":306,"id":"b2:306","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"cultural identity","meaning":"هوية ثقافية","example":"She hoped musical collaboration would build bridges without forcing anyone to abandon cultural identity.","number":307,"id":"b2:307","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"traumatic experience","meaning":"تجربة صادمة","example":"A teenager who had endured a traumatic experience refused to play.","number":308,"id":"b2:308","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"temporary residence","meaning":"إقامة مؤقتة","example":"Some waited months for refugee status and temporary residence.","number":309,"id":"b2:309","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"host community","meaning":"مجتمع مضيف","example":"The host community wanted to help.","number":310,"id":"b2:310","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"social inclusion","meaning":"دمج اجتماعي","example":"Visited schools and spoke about educational access and social inclusion.","number":311,"id":"b2:311","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"psychological","meaning":"دعم نفسي","example":"Nora arranged psychological support and respected his decision.","number":312,"id":"b2:312","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"shared humanity","meaning":"إنسانية مشتركة","example":"Gradually, the musicians discovered shared humanity through rhythm.","number":313,"id":"b2:313","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"build bridges","meaning":"يبني جسور التواصل","example":"She hoped musical collaboration would build bridges without forcing anyone to abandon cultural identity.","number":314,"id":"b2:314","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"musical collaboration","meaning":"تعاون موسيقي","example":"She hoped musical collaboration would build bridges without forcing anyone to abandon cultural identity.","number":315,"id":"b2:315","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"orchestral rehearsal","meaning":"تدريب أوركسترالي","example":"At the first orchestral rehearsal.","number":316,"id":"b2:316","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"cross-cultural","meaning":"صلة بين ثقافات","example":"Cross-cultural connection grew into mutual understanding.","number":317,"id":"b2:317","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"mutual","meaning":"تفاهم متبادل","example":"Cross-cultural connection grew into mutual understanding.","number":318,"id":"b2:318","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"community outreach","meaning":"تواصل مجتمعي","example":"The group organised community outreach.","number":319,"id":"b2:319","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"funding shortage","meaning":"نقص تمويل","example":"Their inclusive event was nearly cancelled because of a funding shortage.","number":320,"id":"b2:320","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"inclusive event","meaning":"فعالية شاملة","example":"Their inclusive event was nearly cancelled because of a funding shortage.","number":321,"id":"b2:321","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"strengthen bonds","meaning":"يعزز الروابط","example":"Their music helped challenge stereotypes and strengthen bonds between families who previously knew little about one another.","number":322,"id":"b2:322","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"challenge","meaning":"يتحدى الصور النمطية","example":"Their music helped challenge stereotypes and strengthen bonds between families who previously knew little about one another.","number":323,"id":"b2:323","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"educational access","meaning":"إتاحة التعليم","example":"Visited schools and spoke about educational access and social inclusion.","number":324,"id":"b2:324","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"},{"term":"sense of dignity","meaning":"إحساس بالكرامة","example":"Nora said the concert had not solved every practical problem, but it had given people a sense of dignity and a place where they could be heard without needing perfect words.","number":325,"id":"b2:325","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-13"}],"story":{"title":"The Refugee Orchestra","paragraphs":["After forced displacement brought several families to a new town, volunteers offered humanitarian assistance and helped them complete an asylum application. Some waited months for refugee status and temporary residence. The host community wanted to help, but a language barrier made everyday communication difficult.","Music teacher Nora proposed an integration programme built around an orchestra. She hoped musical collaboration would build bridges without forcing anyone to abandon cultural identity. At the first orchestral rehearsal, a teenager who had endured a traumatic experience refused to play. Nora arranged psychological support and respected his decision.","Gradually, the musicians discovered shared humanity through rhythm. Cross-cultural connection grew into mutual understanding. The group organised community outreach, visited schools and spoke about educational access and social inclusion. Their inclusive event was nearly cancelled because of a funding shortage, but neighbours supplied equipment and a concert hall.","On performance night, players from many backgrounds stood together. Their music helped challenge stereotypes and strengthen bonds between families who previously knew little about one another. The shy teenager finally joined the last piece. Nora said the concert had not solved every practical problem, but it had given people a sense of dignity and a place where they could be heard without needing perfect words."],"questions":["Why did Nora choose music for the integration programme?","How did she respond to the reluctant teenager?","What nearly prevented the concert?","Why was the concert important beyond entertainment?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-14","title":"The Artistic Rebellion","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 14","level":"B2","set":14,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"cultural censorship","meaning":"رقابة ثقافية","example":"And some councillors demanded cultural censorship.","number":326,"id":"b2:326","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"creative expression","meaning":"تعبير إبداعي","example":"The young artist defended creative expression and artistic freedom.","number":327,"id":"b2:327","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"public exhibition","meaning":"معرض عام","example":"A student gallery announced a public exhibition about life in a changing city.","number":328,"id":"b2:328","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"artistic freedom","meaning":"حرية فنية","example":"The young artist defended creative expression and artistic freedom.","number":329,"id":"b2:329","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"controversial artwork","meaning":"عمل فني مثير للجدل","example":"One controversial artwork used symbolic imagery to criticise the loss of community spaces.","number":330,"id":"b2:330","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"social commentary","meaning":"تعليق اجتماعي نقدي","example":"It offered social commentary through a subtle metaphor.","number":331,"id":"b2:331","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"political satire","meaning":"سخرية سياسية","example":"Others viewed it as political satire that crossed an ethical boundary.","number":332,"id":"b2:332","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"audience","meaning":"تفسير الجمهور","example":"The visual narrative invited audience interpretation rather than presenting a simple political slogan.","number":333,"id":"b2:333","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"challenge convention","meaning":"يتحدى الأعراف","example":"The director argued that cultural norms deserve respect but should not prevent students from trying to challenge convention.","number":334,"id":"b2:334","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"artistic movement","meaning":"حركة فنية","example":"An older critic praised the work's artistic integrity and called it part of a new artistic movement.","number":335,"id":"b2:335","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"provocative message","meaning":"رسالة مستفزة للفكر","example":"Its provocative message caused public controversy.","number":336,"id":"b2:336","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"critical acclaim","meaning":"إشادة نقدية","example":"Some people offered critical acclaim while others remained unconvinced.","number":337,"id":"b2:337","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"artistic integrity","meaning":"نزاهة فنية","example":"An older critic praised the work's artistic integrity and called it part of a new artistic movement.","number":338,"id":"b2:338","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"symbolic imagery","meaning":"صور رمزية","example":"One controversial artwork used symbolic imagery to criticise the loss of community spaces.","number":339,"id":"b2:339","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"cultural norms","meaning":"أعراف ثقافية","example":"The director argued that cultural norms deserve respect but should not prevent students from trying to challenge convention.","number":340,"id":"b2:340","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"defend expression","meaning":"يدافع عن التعبير","example":"The gallery hosted a discussion where visitors could defend expression and question its effects.","number":341,"id":"b2:341","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"ethical boundary","meaning":"حد أخلاقي","example":"Others viewed it as political satire that crossed an ethical boundary.","number":342,"id":"b2:342","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"public controversy","meaning":"جدل عام","example":"Its provocative message caused public controversy.","number":343,"id":"b2:343","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"subtle metaphor","meaning":"استعارة دقيقة","example":"It offered social commentary through a subtle metaphor.","number":344,"id":"b2:344","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"visual narrative","meaning":"سرد بصري","example":"The visual narrative invited audience interpretation rather than presenting a simple political slogan.","number":345,"id":"b2:345","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"creative","meaning":"استقلال إبداعي","example":"The young artist defended creative expression and artistic freedom.","number":346,"id":"b2:346","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"social criticism","meaning":"نقد اجتماعي","example":"Even social criticism can be expressed without insulting people personally.","number":347,"id":"b2:347","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"unexpected reaction","meaning":"رد فعل غير متوقع","example":"Unexpected reaction turned into meaningful dialogue.","number":348,"id":"b2:348","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"meaningful dialogue","meaning":"حوار ذو معنى","example":"Unexpected reaction turned into meaningful dialogue.","number":349,"id":"b2:349","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"},{"term":"cultural influence","meaning":"تأثير ثقافي","example":"She discovered that cultural influence does not come from forcing everyone to agree.","number":350,"id":"b2:350","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-14"}],"story":{"title":"The Artistic Rebellion","paragraphs":["A student gallery announced a public exhibition about life in a changing city. One controversial artwork used symbolic imagery to criticise the loss of community spaces. Its provocative message caused public controversy, and some councillors demanded cultural censorship.","The young artist defended creative expression and artistic freedom. Her painting was not merely decoration: it offered social commentary through a subtle metaphor. A broken window represented lost trust, while a small plant symbolised hope. The visual narrative invited audience interpretation rather than presenting a simple political slogan.","An older critic praised the work's artistic integrity and called it part of a new artistic movement. Others viewed it as political satire that crossed an ethical boundary. The director argued that cultural norms deserve respect but should not prevent students from trying to challenge convention. Even social criticism can be expressed without insulting people personally.","The gallery hosted a discussion where visitors could defend expression and question its effects. Unexpected reaction turned into meaningful dialogue. Some people offered critical acclaim while others remained unconvinced. The artist protected her creative independence but listened carefully to her neighbours. She discovered that cultural influence does not come from forcing everyone to agree. Sometimes art succeeds by encouraging people to examine familiar ideas from an unfamiliar perspective."],"questions":["What did the broken window and small plant represent?","Why did some councillors call for censorship?","How did the gallery handle disagreement?","What does the story imply about artistic influence?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-15","title":"The Hospital Decision","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 15","level":"B2","set":15,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"medical consent","meaning":"موافقة طبية","example":"The lead physician explained medical consent and patient autonomy to the family.","number":351,"id":"b2:351","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"clinical judgement","meaning":"حكم سريري","example":"Good clinical judgement, she argued, includes listening as well as diagnosis.","number":352,"id":"b2:352","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"patient autonomy","meaning":"استقلالية المريض","example":"The lead physician explained medical consent and patient autonomy to the family.","number":353,"id":"b2:353","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"ethical consultation","meaning":"استشارة أخلاقية","example":"The team requested an ethical consultation from the medical ethics committee.","number":354,"id":"b2:354","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"life-threatening","meaning":"حالة تهدد الحياة","example":"A teenager arrived at hospital with a life-threatening condition.","number":355,"id":"b2:355","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"treatment options","meaning":"خيارات علاجية","example":"Doctors considered several treatment options.","number":356,"id":"b2:356","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"potential side effects","meaning":"آثار جانبية محتملة","example":"Each with potential side effects.","number":357,"id":"b2:357","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"clinical evidence","meaning":"أدلة سريرية","example":"Their clinical evidence supported an urgent intervention.","number":358,"id":"b2:358","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"urgent intervention","meaning":"تدخل عاجل","example":"Their clinical evidence supported an urgent intervention.","number":359,"id":"b2:359","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"informed decision","meaning":"قرار واع","example":"Through shared decision-making, the family and medical team reached an informed decision that the teenager could understand.","number":360,"id":"b2:360","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"family wishes","meaning":"رغبات الأسرة","example":"While the patient's own family wishes were less clear.","number":361,"id":"b2:361","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"medical uncertainty","meaning":"عدم يقين طبي","example":"Its members discussed medical uncertainty.","number":362,"id":"b2:362","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"professional duty","meaning":"واجب مهني","example":"She used a compassionate approach and explained the professional duty to act safely without ignoring the patient's voice.","number":363,"id":"b2:363","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"communicate risks","meaning":"يوضح المخاطر","example":"A nurse urged everyone to communicate risks honestly.","number":364,"id":"b2:364","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"recovery prospects","meaning":"آفاق التعافي","example":"Diagnostic accuracy and the patient's recovery prospects.","number":365,"id":"b2:365","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"supportive care","meaning":"رعاية داعمة","example":"Another offered supportive care with a different balance of quality of life and risk.","number":366,"id":"b2:366","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"medical ethics","meaning":"لجنة أخلاقيات طبية","example":"The team requested an ethical consultation from the medical ethics committee.","number":367,"id":"b2:367","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"legal guardian","meaning":"وصي قانوني","example":"The legal guardian believed the quickest treatment was always best.","number":368,"id":"b2:368","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"quality of life","meaning":"جودة الحياة","example":"Another offered supportive care with a different balance of quality of life and risk.","number":369,"id":"b2:369","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"diagnostic accuracy","meaning":"دقة التشخيص","example":"Diagnostic accuracy and the patient's recovery prospects.","number":370,"id":"b2:370","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"intensive care","meaning":"عناية مركزة","example":"One plan involved intensive care and might improve survival but place an emotional burden on the family.","number":371,"id":"b2:371","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"patient","meaning":"سرية المريض","example":"They also emphasised patient confidentiality.","number":372,"id":"b2:372","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"emotional burden","meaning":"عبء عاطفي","example":"One plan involved intensive care and might improve survival but place an emotional burden on the family.","number":373,"id":"b2:373","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"compassionate","meaning":"نهج رحيم","example":"She used a compassionate approach and explained the professional duty to act safely without ignoring the patient's voice.","number":374,"id":"b2:374","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"},{"term":"shared","meaning":"صنع قرار مشترك","example":"Through shared decision-making, the family and medical team reached an informed decision that the teenager could understand.","number":375,"id":"b2:375","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-15"}],"story":{"title":"The Hospital Decision","paragraphs":["A teenager arrived at hospital with a life-threatening condition. Doctors considered several treatment options, each with potential side effects. Their clinical evidence supported an urgent intervention, but the teenager was frightened and wanted more time.","The lead physician explained medical consent and patient autonomy to the family. The legal guardian believed the quickest treatment was always best, while the patient's own family wishes were less clear. A nurse urged everyone to communicate risks honestly. Good clinical judgement, she argued, includes listening as well as diagnosis.","The team requested an ethical consultation from the medical ethics committee. They also emphasised patient confidentiality. Its members discussed medical uncertainty, diagnostic accuracy and the patient's recovery prospects. One plan involved intensive care and might improve survival but place an emotional burden on the family. Another offered supportive care with a different balance of quality of life and risk.","The doctor avoided making promises. She used a compassionate approach and explained the professional duty to act safely without ignoring the patient's voice. Through shared decision-making, the family and medical team reached an informed decision that the teenager could understand. The story reminded everyone that medical skill alone cannot settle every difficult choice. Respect and clarity are also essential when the future is uncertain."],"questions":["Why was the treatment decision difficult?","What did the ethics committee add to the discussion?","How did the physician communicate responsibly?","What does shared decision-making require?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-16","title":"The Climate Engineering Trial","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 16","level":"B2","set":16,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"geoengineering","meaning":"هندسة المناخ","example":"A university proposed geoengineering to slow rising global temperature.","number":376,"id":"b2:376","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"carbon removal","meaning":"إزالة الكربون","example":"Its research proposal described a proposed intervention involving atmospheric particles while testing a separate carbon removal system.","number":377,"id":"b2:377","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"atmospheric","meaning":"جسيمات جوية","example":"Its research proposal described a proposed intervention involving atmospheric particles while testing a separate carbon removal system.","number":378,"id":"b2:378","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"proposed","meaning":"تدخل مقترح","example":"A university proposed geoengineering to slow rising global temperature.","number":379,"id":"b2:379","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"scientific trial","meaning":"تجربة علمية","example":"Supporters described the scientific trial as an emergency measure.","number":380,"id":"b2:380","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"unintended side","meaning":"أثر جانبي غير مقصود","example":"Supporters described the scientific trial as an emergency measure, but critics warned that an irreversible change might have an unintended side effect.","number":381,"id":"b2:381","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"environmental risk","meaning":"خطر بيئي","example":"However, the evidence gap was large and the environmental risk uncertain.","number":382,"id":"b2:382","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"global temperature","meaning":"درجة الحرارة العالمية","example":"A university proposed geoengineering to slow rising global temperature.","number":383,"id":"b2:383","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"climate modelling","meaning":"نمذجة المناخ","example":"Professor Chen used climate modelling to estimate potential benefits.","number":384,"id":"b2:384","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"research proposal","meaning":"مقترح بحثي","example":"Its research proposal described a proposed intervention involving atmospheric particles while testing a separate carbon removal system.","number":385,"id":"b2:385","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"evidence gap","meaning":"فجوة في الأدلة","example":"However, the evidence gap was large and the environmental risk uncertain.","number":386,"id":"b2:386","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"public consultation","meaning":"مشاورة عامة","example":"At a public consultation, students challenged the project's funding controversy and asked who would provide ethical oversight.","number":387,"id":"b2:387","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"scientific integrity","meaning":"نزاهة علمية","example":"The professor defended scientific integrity and a precautionary approach.","number":388,"id":"b2:388","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"precautionary","meaning":"نهج احترازي","example":"The professor defended scientific integrity and a precautionary approach.","number":389,"id":"b2:389","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"irreversible change","meaning":"تغير لا يمكن عكسه","example":"Supporters described the scientific trial as an emergency measure, but critics warned that an irreversible change might have an unintended side effect.","number":390,"id":"b2:390","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"long-term monitoring","meaning":"رصد طويل الأجل","example":"The plan required long-term monitoring.","number":391,"id":"b2:391","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"independent","meaning":"تقييم مستقل","example":"The plan required long-term monitoring, independent evaluation and global coordination because air does not respect national borders.","number":392,"id":"b2:392","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"potential benefits","meaning":"فوائد محتملة","example":"Professor Chen used climate modelling to estimate potential benefits.","number":393,"id":"b2:393","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"unequal effects","meaning":"آثار غير متساوية","example":"One region might benefit while another suffered unequal effects.","number":394,"id":"b2:394","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"funding controversy","meaning":"جدل حول التمويل","example":"At a public consultation, students challenged the project's funding controversy and asked who would provide ethical oversight.","number":395,"id":"b2:395","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"ethical oversight","meaning":"رقابة أخلاقية","example":"At a public consultation, students challenged the project's funding controversy and asked who would provide ethical oversight.","number":396,"id":"b2:396","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"emergency measure","meaning":"إجراء طارئ","example":"Supporters described the scientific trial as an emergency measure.","number":397,"id":"b2:397","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"scientific debate","meaning":"جدل علمي","example":"The university postponed any outdoor experiment and expanded its scientific debate.","number":398,"id":"b2:398","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"global coordination","meaning":"تنسيق عالمي","example":"The plan required long-term monitoring, independent evaluation and global coordination because air does not respect national borders.","number":399,"id":"b2:399","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"},{"term":"responsible","meaning":"ابتكار مسؤول","example":"This decision disappointed some researchers, but the professor believed responsible innovation could not depend on silence.","number":400,"id":"b2:400","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-16"}],"story":{"title":"The Climate Engineering Trial","paragraphs":["A university proposed geoengineering to slow rising global temperature. Its research proposal described a proposed intervention involving atmospheric particles while testing a separate carbon removal system. Supporters described the scientific trial as an emergency measure, but critics warned that an irreversible change might have an unintended side effect. Professor Chen used climate modelling to estimate potential benefits. However, the evidence gap was large and the environmental risk uncertain.","One region might benefit while another suffered unequal effects. The plan required long-term monitoring, independent evaluation and global coordination because air does not respect national borders. At a public consultation, students challenged the project's funding controversy and asked who would provide ethical oversight. The professor defended scientific integrity and a precautionary approach. She agreed that public concern was reasonable, even when it slowed research.","The debate was not simply about whether the invention worked; it was also about who would bear the consequences. The university postponed any outdoor experiment and expanded its scientific debate. Instead of dismissing critics, it invited them to test the assumptions. This decision disappointed some researchers, but the professor believed responsible innovation could not depend on silence. New technology may offer solutions, she said, yet its risks must be examined before society is asked to accept them."],"questions":["Why did critics fear geoengineering even if it lowered temperature?","Why was global coordination necessary?","How did the university respond to public concerns?","What principle guided the final decision?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-17","title":"The Arctic Research Station","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 17","level":"B2","set":17,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"permafrost","meaning":"تربة صقيعية دائمة","example":"A field researcher noticed unusual cracks in the permafrost.","number":401,"id":"b2:401","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"polar ecosystem","meaning":"نظام بيئي قطبي","example":"Threatening the polar ecosystem.","number":402,"id":"b2:402","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"melting ice sheet","meaning":"غطاء جليدي ذائب","example":"A melting ice sheet appeared to be retreating faster than expected.","number":403,"id":"b2:403","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"seasonal variation","meaning":"تغير موسمي","example":"The scientists studied seasonal variation and each weather pattern before linking a gradual thaw to rising sea level.","number":404,"id":"b2:404","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"weather pattern","meaning":"نمط طقس","example":"The scientists studied seasonal variation and each weather pattern before linking a gradual thaw to rising sea level.","number":405,"id":"b2:405","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"research outpost","meaning":"محطة بحث نائية","example":"At a remote research outpost.","number":406,"id":"b2:406","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"thermal insulation","meaning":"عزل حراري","example":"The station relied on thermal insulation and regular deliveries.","number":407,"id":"b2:407","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"rising sea level","meaning":"ارتفاع مستوى البحر","example":"The scientists studied seasonal variation and each weather pattern before linking a gradual thaw to rising sea level.","number":408,"id":"b2:408","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"field measurements","meaning":"قياسات ميدانية","example":"They took field measurements and treated the cracks as an environmental indicator, not automatic proof of one explanation.","number":409,"id":"b2:409","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"environmental","meaning":"مؤشر بيئي","example":"They took field measurements and treated the cracks as an environmental indicator, not automatic proof of one explanation.","number":410,"id":"b2:410","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"extreme isolation","meaning":"عزلة شديدة","example":"Extreme isolation made the work difficult.","number":411,"id":"b2:411","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"satellite imagery","meaning":"صور الأقمار الصناعية","example":"The team used satellite imagery and remote sensing to compare the frozen landscape with historical records.","number":412,"id":"b2:412","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"field researcher","meaning":"باحث ميداني","example":"A field researcher noticed unusual","number":413,"id":"b2:413","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"frozen landscape","meaning":"مشهد طبيعي متجمد","example":"The team used satellite imagery and remote sensing to compare the frozen landscape with historical records.","number":414,"id":"b2:414","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"climate evidence","meaning":"دليل مناخي","example":"The team compared the new climate evidence with a historical trend and offered a cautious interpretation.","number":415,"id":"b2:415","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"gradual thaw","meaning":"ذوبان تدريجي","example":"The scientists studied seasonal variation and each weather pattern before linking a gradual thaw to rising sea level.","number":416,"id":"b2:416","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"remote sensing","meaning":"استشعار عن بعد","example":"The team used satellite imagery and remote sensing to compare the frozen landscape with historical records.","number":417,"id":"b2:417","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"instrument","meaning":"عطل جهاز قياس","example":"But an instrument malfunction had also affected the temperature readings.","number":418,"id":"b2:418","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"scientific sample","meaning":"عينة علمية","example":"A scientific sample suggested warming.","number":419,"id":"b2:419","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"research","meaning":"تعاون بحثي","example":"At a remote research outpost, a field researcher noticed unusual cracks in the permafrost.","number":420,"id":"b2:420","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"unexpected","meaning":"ملاحظة غير متوقعة","example":"An unexpected observation showed that one valley warmed differently from a nearby region.","number":421,"id":"b2:421","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"historical trend","meaning":"اتجاه تاريخي","example":"The team compared the new climate evidence with a historical trend and offered a cautious interpretation.","number":422,"id":"b2:422","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"accurate","meaning":"قياس دقيق","example":"Engineers corrected the device and obtained an accurate measurement.","number":423,"id":"b2:423","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"cautious","meaning":"تفسير حذر","example":"The team compared the new climate evidence with a historical trend and offered a cautious interpretation.","number":424,"id":"b2:424","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"},{"term":"publish findings","meaning":"ينشر النتائج","example":"Only after repeated checks did they publish findings.","number":425,"id":"b2:425","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-17"}],"story":{"title":"The Arctic Research Station","paragraphs":["At a remote research outpost, a field researcher noticed unusual cracks in the permafrost. A melting ice sheet appeared to be retreating faster than expected, threatening the polar ecosystem. The team used satellite imagery and remote sensing to compare the frozen landscape with historical records.","The scientists studied seasonal variation and each weather pattern before linking a gradual thaw to rising sea level. They took field measurements and treated the cracks as an environmental indicator, not automatic proof of one explanation. A scientific sample suggested warming, but an instrument malfunction had also affected the temperature readings.","Extreme isolation made the work difficult. The station relied on thermal insulation and regular deliveries, so a small technical failure could interrupt the whole project. Through research collaboration, engineers corrected the device and obtained an accurate measurement. An unexpected observation showed that one valley warmed differently from a nearby region.","The team compared the new climate evidence with a historical trend and offered a cautious interpretation. They refused to claim that a single local result could describe the entire Arctic. Only after repeated checks did they publish findings. Their leader reminded the students watching online that science is strongest when researchers describe both what their measurements show and what those measurements cannot yet explain."],"questions":["Why did the researchers avoid an immediate conclusion?","What did comparing valleys reveal?","How did research collaboration improve the data?","What lesson about scientific claims is emphasised?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-18","title":"The Last Printed Newspaper","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 18","level":"B2","set":18,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"digital transition","meaning":"انتقال رقمي","example":"The editor proposed a digital transition with an online platform and a new subscription model.","number":426,"id":"b2:426","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"print circulation","meaning":"توزيع الصحف المطبوعة","example":"But its print circulation was falling.","number":427,"id":"b2:427","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"reader loyalty","meaning":"ولاء القراء","example":"Others believed a digital archive and faster local reporting might strengthen reader loyalty.","number":428,"id":"b2:428","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"subscription model","meaning":"نموذج اشتراك","example":"The editor proposed a digital transition with an online platform and a new subscription model.","number":429,"id":"b2:429","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"advertising revenue","meaning":"عائد إعلاني","example":"Declining readership and reduced advertising revenue threatened financial sustainability.","number":430,"id":"b2:430","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"editorial policy","meaning":"سياسة تحريرية","example":"Some staff feared that audience analytics would replace editorial policy.","number":431,"id":"b2:431","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"investigative feature","meaning":"تحقيق صحفي مطول","example":"An investigative feature series and community journalism.","number":432,"id":"b2:432","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"local reporting","meaning":"تغطية محلية","example":"Others believed a digital archive and faster local reporting might strengthen reader loyalty.","number":433,"id":"b2:433","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"independent press","meaning":"صحافة مستقلة","example":"The paper had earned respect through independent press coverage.","number":434,"id":"b2:434","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"misinformation","meaning":"حملة تضليل","example":"It also taught media literacy during a misinformation campaign that had confused residents.","number":435,"id":"b2:435","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"community","meaning":"صحافة مجتمعية","example":"An investigative feature series and community journalism.","number":436,"id":"b2:436","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"newsroom culture","meaning":"ثقافة غرفة الأخبار","example":"The newsroom culture changed as younger reporters suggested interactive storytelling and public engagement events.","number":437,"id":"b2:437","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"public engagement","meaning":"تفاعل الجمهور","example":"The newsroom culture changed as younger reporters suggested interactive storytelling and public engagement events.","number":438,"id":"b2:438","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"online platform","meaning":"منصة إلكترونية","example":"The editor proposed a digital transition with an online platform and a new subscription model.","number":439,"id":"b2:439","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"financial","meaning":"استدامة مالية","example":"Declining readership and reduced advertising revenue threatened financial sustainability.","number":440,"id":"b2:440","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"declining readership","meaning":"تراجع عدد القراء","example":"Declining readership and reduced advertising revenue threatened financial sustainability.","number":441,"id":"b2:441","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"journalistic","meaning":"معايير صحفية","example":"The editor insisted on journalistic standards.","number":442,"id":"b2:442","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"reliable information","meaning":"معلومات موثوقة","example":"A credible outlet must provide reliable information regardless of format.","number":443,"id":"b2:443","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"digital archive","meaning":"أرشيف رقمي","example":"Others believed a digital archive and faster local reporting might strengthen reader loyalty.","number":444,"id":"b2:444","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"print edition","meaning":"نسخة مطبوعة","example":"A smaller print edition would remain for residents who preferred paper.","number":445,"id":"b2:445","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"audience analytics","meaning":"تحليلات الجمهور","example":"Some staff feared that audience analytics would replace editorial policy.","number":446,"id":"b2:446","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"adapt to change","meaning":"يتكيف مع التغيير","example":"The staff learned to adapt to change without abandoning the reason the newspaper existed.","number":447,"id":"b2:447","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"credible outlet","meaning":"وسيلة إعلام موثوقة","example":"A credible outlet must provide reliable information regardless of format.","number":448,"id":"b2:448","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"behind-the-scenes","meaning":"ما وراء الكواليس","example":"She invited readers to a behind-the-scenes meeting.","number":449,"id":"b2:449","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"},{"term":"media literacy","meaning":"ثقافة إعلامية","example":"It also taught media literacy during a misinformation campaign that had confused residents.","number":450,"id":"b2:450","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-18"}],"story":{"title":"The Last Printed Newspaper","paragraphs":["The town newspaper had survived for ninety years, but its print circulation was falling. Declining readership and reduced advertising revenue threatened financial sustainability. The editor proposed a digital transition with an online platform and a new subscription model.","Some staff feared that audience analytics would replace editorial policy. Others believed a digital archive and faster local reporting might strengthen reader loyalty. The paper had earned respect through independent press coverage, an investigative feature series and community journalism. It also taught media literacy during a misinformation campaign that had confused residents.","The newsroom culture changed as younger reporters suggested interactive storytelling and public engagement events. The editor insisted on journalistic standards: a credible outlet must provide reliable information regardless of format. She invited readers to a behind-the-scenes meeting, showing how an article was checked before publication.","After listening, the team chose a hybrid approach. A smaller print edition would remain for residents who preferred paper, while a digital service would support future growth. The staff learned to adapt to change without abandoning the reason the newspaper existed. The editor said the real product was never ink or a screen. It was the trust between a town and the people who reported its stories."],"questions":["What financial pressures forced change at the newspaper?","What did some staff worry digital tools might weaken?","Why did the newspaper keep a smaller print edition?","What did the editor identify as the newspaper’s true value?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-19","title":"The Election Night Puzzle","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 19","level":"B2","set":19,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"electoral system","meaning":"نظام انتخابي","example":"The electoral system allowed an election observer to examine the records.","number":451,"id":"b2:451","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"turnout rate","meaning":"نسبة الإقبال على التصويت","example":"The turnout rate in one electoral district suddenly fell.","number":452,"id":"b2:452","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"voter suppression","meaning":"إعاقة التصويت","example":"Local volunteers feared voter suppression.","number":453,"id":"b2:453","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"electoral district","meaning":"دائرة انتخابية","example":"The turnout rate in one electoral district suddenly fell.","number":454,"id":"b2:454","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"coalition government","meaning":"حكومة ائتلافية","example":"One independent candidate accused the coalition government of planning the closure, but there was no proof of a deliberate scheme.","number":455,"id":"b2:455","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"policy proposal","meaning":"مقترح سياسة","example":"During a public debate, candidates discussed an electoral reform and a policy proposal for emergency voting arrangements.","number":456,"id":"b2:456","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"public mandate","meaning":"تفويض شعبي","example":"Leaders accepted the public mandate and supported a peaceful transition once accurate results were confirmed.","number":457,"id":"b2:457","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"independent","meaning":"مرشح مستقل","example":"One independent candidate accused the coalition government of planning the closure, but there was no proof of a deliberate scheme.","number":458,"id":"b2:458","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"political rhetoric","meaning":"خطاب سياسي","example":"Political rhetoric made the disagreement worse.","number":459,"id":"b2:459","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"electoral reform","meaning":"إصلاح انتخابي","example":"During a public debate, candidates discussed an electoral reform and a policy proposal for emergency voting arrangements.","number":460,"id":"b2:460","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"public debate","meaning":"نقاش عام","example":"During a public debate, candidates discussed an electoral reform and a policy proposal for emergency voting arrangements.","number":461,"id":"b2:461","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"campaign strategy","meaning":"استراتيجية حملة","example":"The campaign strategy of blaming opponents attracted attention.","number":462,"id":"b2:462","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"credible promise","meaning":"وعد موثوق","example":"Residents wanted a transparent process, an accountability mechanism and a credible promise that they could exercise their rights.","number":463,"id":"b2:463","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"accountability","meaning":"آلية مساءلة","example":"Residents wanted a transparent process, an accountability mechanism and a credible promise that they could exercise their rights.","number":464,"id":"b2:464","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"transparent process","meaning":"عملية شفافة","example":"Residents wanted a transparent process.","number":465,"id":"b2:465","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"election observer","meaning":"مراقب انتخابات","example":"The electoral system allowed an election observer to examine the records.","number":466,"id":"b2:466","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"demographic shift","meaning":"تحول سكاني","example":"She compared demographic shift data with the previous year and found misleading statistics in a widely shared message.","number":467,"id":"b2:467","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"misleading statistics","meaning":"إحصاءات مضللة","example":"She compared demographic shift data with the previous year and found misleading statistics in a widely shared message.","number":468,"id":"b2:468","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"polling station","meaning":"إغلاق مركز اقتراع","example":"A polling station closure had prevented hundreds of residents from voting.","number":469,"id":"b2:469","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"widespread concern","meaning":"قلق واسع","example":"The disputed figures produced a contested result and widespread concern.","number":470,"id":"b2:470","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"public confidence","meaning":"ثقة عامة","example":"Yet it did little to restore public confidence.","number":471,"id":"b2:471","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"contested result","meaning":"نتيجة محل نزاع","example":"The disputed figures produced a contested result and widespread concern.","number":472,"id":"b2:472","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"peaceful transition","meaning":"انتقال سلمي","example":"Leaders accepted the public mandate and supported a peaceful transition once accurate results were confirmed.","number":473,"id":"b2:473","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"constitutional","meaning":"مبدأ دستوري","example":"The observer praised democratic participation and respect for a constitutional principle: political competition should not destroy the fairness of the rules.","number":474,"id":"b2:474","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"},{"term":"democratic","meaning":"مشاركة ديمقراطية","example":"The observer praised democratic participation and respect for a constitutional principle: political competition should not destroy the fairness of the rules.","number":475,"id":"b2:475","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-19"}],"story":{"title":"The Election Night Puzzle","paragraphs":["On election night, the turnout rate in one electoral district suddenly fell. A polling station closure had prevented hundreds of residents from voting. Local volunteers feared voter suppression, while officials said a technical fault had caused the problem.","The electoral system allowed an election observer to examine the records. She compared demographic shift data with the previous year and found misleading statistics in a widely shared message. Political rhetoric made the disagreement worse. One independent candidate accused the coalition government of planning the closure, but there was no proof of a deliberate scheme.","During a public debate, candidates discussed an electoral reform and a policy proposal for emergency voting arrangements. The campaign strategy of blaming opponents attracted attention, yet it did little to restore public confidence. Residents wanted a transparent process, an accountability mechanism and a credible promise that they could exercise their rights.","The disputed figures produced a contested result and widespread concern. A neutral review recommended a new vote in the affected district. Leaders accepted the public mandate and supported a peaceful transition once accurate results were confirmed. The observer praised democratic participation and respect for a constitutional principle: political competition should not destroy the fairness of the rules. She reminded everyone that elections are not only contests to win but shared responsibilities to protect."],"questions":["Why did the turnout rate suddenly fall?","Why was blaming the government premature?","What solution restored public confidence?","What larger democratic principle does the story defend?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-20","title":"The Historic Bridge Collapse","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 20","level":"B2","set":20,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"structural weakness","meaning":"ضعف هيكلي","example":"Student engineer Zara noticed a structural weakness in an old railway bridge.","number":476,"id":"b2:476","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"load-bearing beam","meaning":"عارضة حاملة للأحمال","example":"A load-bearing beam had developed a small crack.","number":477,"id":"b2:477","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"engineering","meaning":"تقصير هندسي","example":"She asked her teacher to compare the design specification with current engineering standards.","number":478,"id":"b2:478","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"material fatigue","meaning":"إجهاد المواد","example":"Possibly caused by material fatigue.","number":479,"id":"b2:479","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"inspection report","meaning":"تقرير تفتيش","example":"The latest inspection report called it harmless.","number":480,"id":"b2:480","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"stress test","meaning":"اختبار تحمل","example":"A stress test suggested the structure could fail under heavy traffic.","number":481,"id":"b2:481","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"bridge closure","meaning":"إغلاق جسر","example":"Although a bridge closure would cause inconvenience.","number":482,"id":"b2:482","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"safety violation","meaning":"مخالفة سلامة","example":"Ignoring a safety violation could be disastrous.","number":483,"id":"b2:483","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"engineering","meaning":"معايير هندسية","example":"She asked her teacher to compare the design specification with current engineering standards.","number":484,"id":"b2:484","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"construction flaw","meaning":"عيب إنشائي","example":"The latest inspection report called it harmless, but Zara worried about a construction flaw and possible engineering oversight.","number":485,"id":"b2:485","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"maintenance","meaning":"جدول صيانة","example":"The local authority ordered a damage assessment and examined the maintenance schedule.","number":486,"id":"b2:486","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"repair estimate","meaning":"تقدير تكلفة الإصلاح","example":"Their repair estimate was high.","number":487,"id":"b2:487","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"structural integrity","meaning":"سلامة الهيكل","example":"Zara explained the importance of structural integrity and a long-term solution.","number":488,"id":"b2:488","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"public inquiry","meaning":"تحقيق عام","example":"During a public inquiry, engineers presented preliminary findings and expert testimony.","number":489,"id":"b2:489","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"preliminary findings","meaning":"نتائج أولية","example":"Engineers presented preliminary findings and expert testimony.","number":490,"id":"b2:490","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"expert testimony","meaning":"شهادة خبير","example":"Engineers presented preliminary findings and expert testimony.","number":491,"id":"b2:491","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"design specification","meaning":"مواصفات التصميم","example":"She asked her teacher to compare the design specification with current engineering standards.","number":492,"id":"b2:492","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"pressure fracture","meaning":"تصدع بسبب الضغط","example":"An independent audit confirmed a pressure fracture.","number":493,"id":"b2:493","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"risk mitigation","meaning":"تخفيف المخاطر","example":"Yet risk mitigation required more than a quick patch.","number":494,"id":"b2:494","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"emergency response","meaning":"استجابة طارئة","example":"The council approved an emergency response route to restore access while planning a rebuilding project.","number":495,"id":"b2:495","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"restore access","meaning":"يعيد إتاحة العبور","example":"The council approved an emergency response route to restore access while planning a rebuilding project.","number":496,"id":"b2:496","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"long-term solution","meaning":"حل طويل الأمد","example":"Zara explained the importance of structural integrity and a long-term solution.","number":497,"id":"b2:497","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"independent audit","meaning":"تدقيق مستقل","example":"An independent audit confirmed a pressure fracture.","number":498,"id":"b2:498","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"prevent a disaster","meaning":"يمنع كارثة","example":"By closing the bridge, the town had managed to prevent a disaster rather than waiting for a full collapse.","number":499,"id":"b2:499","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"},{"term":"rebuilding project","meaning":"مشروع إعادة بناء","example":"The council approved an emergency response route to restore access while planning a rebuilding project.","number":500,"id":"b2:500","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-20"}],"story":{"title":"The Historic Bridge Collapse","paragraphs":["Student engineer Zara noticed a structural weakness in an old railway bridge. A load-bearing beam had developed a small crack, possibly caused by material fatigue. The latest inspection report called it harmless, but Zara worried about a construction flaw and possible engineering oversight.","She asked her teacher to compare the design specification with current engineering standards. A stress test suggested the structure could fail under heavy traffic. Although a bridge closure would cause inconvenience, ignoring a safety violation could be disastrous. The local authority ordered a damage assessment and examined the maintenance schedule.","An independent audit confirmed a pressure fracture. During a public inquiry, engineers presented preliminary findings and expert testimony. Their repair estimate was high, yet risk mitigation required more than a quick patch. The council approved an emergency response route to restore access while planning a rebuilding project.","Some residents complained about the delay. Zara explained the importance of structural integrity and a long-term solution. By closing the bridge, the town had managed to prevent a disaster rather than waiting for a full collapse. The incident changed the school club's view of engineering: good design is not only about creating impressive structures. It is about being willing to question old assumptions before people's safety depends on them."],"questions":["What made Zara question the original inspection report?","Why was closing the bridge justified?","What did the independent audit contribute?","What does the story suggest about engineering responsibility?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-21","title":"The Global Food Shortage","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 21","level":"B2","set":21,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"crop failure","meaning":"فشل المحصول","example":"After unpredictable rainfall caused crop failure in several countries.","number":501,"id":"b2:501","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"supply chain","meaning":"اضطراب سلسلة الإمداد","example":"And a supply chain disruption produced a severe shortage of imported grain.","number":502,"id":"b2:502","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"food insecurity","meaning":"انعدام الأمن الغذائي","example":"Food insecurity spread rapidly.","number":503,"id":"b2:503","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"agricultural yield","meaning":"غلة زراعية","example":"The agricultural yield fell.","number":504,"id":"b2:504","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"severe shortage","meaning":"نقص حاد","example":"And a supply chain disruption produced a severe shortage of imported grain.","number":505,"id":"b2:505","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"unpredictable","meaning":"أمطار غير متوقعة","example":"After unpredictable rainfall caused crop failure in several countries.","number":506,"id":"b2:506","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"soil depletion","meaning":"استنزاف التربة","example":"An international team studied soil depletion and the effects of weak climate resilience.","number":507,"id":"b2:507","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"sustainable farming","meaning":"زراعة مستدامة","example":"But sustainable farming would help prevent future crises.","number":508,"id":"b2:508","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"farming subsidy","meaning":"دعم زراعي","example":"Local producers asked for a farming subsidy to test new methods.","number":509,"id":"b2:509","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"price inflation","meaning":"ارتفاع الأسعار","example":"Families faced price inflation.","number":510,"id":"b2:510","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"food distribution","meaning":"توزيع الغذاء","example":"Emergency reserves could support food distribution now.","number":511,"id":"b2:511","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"emergency reserves","meaning":"احتياطيات الطوارئ","example":"Emergency reserves could support food distribution now.","number":512,"id":"b2:512","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"imported grain","meaning":"حبوب مستوردة","example":"The agricultural yield fell, and a supply chain disruption produced a severe shortage of imported grain.","number":513,"id":"b2:513","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"local producers","meaning":"منتجون محليون","example":"Local producers asked for a farming subsidy to test new methods.","number":514,"id":"b2:514","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"food waste reduction","meaning":"تقليل هدر الطعام","example":"Students proposed farming innovation, a nutrition programme and food waste reduction to use existing supplies more efficiently.","number":515,"id":"b2:515","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"farming innovation","meaning":"ابتكار زراعي","example":"Students proposed farming innovation.","number":516,"id":"b2:516","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"equitable access","meaning":"وصول عادل","example":"The council committed to equitable access and a transparent distribution process.","number":517,"id":"b2:517","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"nutrition programme","meaning":"برنامج تغذية","example":"Students proposed farming innovation, a nutrition programme and food waste reduction to use existing supplies more efficiently.","number":518,"id":"b2:518","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"economic hardship","meaning":"ضائقة اقتصادية","example":"Especially in areas already suffering economic hardship.","number":519,"id":"b2:519","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"climate resilience","meaning":"القدرة على مواجهة المناخ","example":"An international team studied soil depletion and the effects of weak climate resilience.","number":520,"id":"b2:520","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"cross-border trade","meaning":"تجارة عابرة للحدود","example":"They also examined cross-border trade.","number":521,"id":"b2:521","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"vulnerable","meaning":"أسر هشة","example":"They also examined cross-border trade, warning that sudden export bans might protect one market while harming vulnerable households elsewhere.","number":522,"id":"b2:522","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"urgent relief","meaning":"إغاثة عاجلة","example":"The team argued that both urgent relief and long-term food security mattered.","number":523,"id":"b2:523","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"market speculation","meaning":"مضاربة في السوق","example":"Some politicians blamed market speculation.","number":524,"id":"b2:524","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"},{"term":"policy intervention","meaning":"تدخل سياسي تنظيمي","example":"Others demanded an immediate policy intervention.","number":525,"id":"b2:525","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-21"}],"story":{"title":"The Global Food Shortage","paragraphs":["After unpredictable rainfall caused crop failure in several countries, food insecurity spread rapidly. The agricultural yield fell, and a supply chain disruption produced a severe shortage of imported grain. Families faced price inflation, especially in areas already suffering economic hardship.","An international team studied soil depletion and the effects of weak climate resilience. Some politicians blamed market speculation; others demanded an immediate policy intervention. The team argued that both urgent relief and long-term food security mattered. Emergency reserves could support food distribution now, but sustainable farming would help prevent future crises.","Local producers asked for a farming subsidy to test new methods. Students proposed farming innovation, a nutrition programme and food waste reduction to use existing supplies more efficiently. They also examined cross-border trade, warning that sudden export bans might protect one market while harming vulnerable households elsewhere.","The council committed to equitable access and a transparent distribution process. No single measure removed the crisis, but better cooperation improved daily life. The project leader told students that hunger is not simply a problem of growing more crops. It also concerns affordability, fairness, infrastructure and the political choices that determine who receives help first."],"questions":["What chain of events caused the food shortage?","Why were emergency reserves not enough by themselves?","How could export bans harm other communities?","What does the leader mean by calling hunger a fairness issue?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-22","title":"The Psychology of Advertising","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 22","level":"B2","set":22,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"persuasive technique","meaning":"أسلوب إقناع","example":"Its persuasive technique was simple.","number":526,"id":"b2:526","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"emotional appeal","meaning":"تأثير عاطفي","example":"An emotional appeal connected the product with friendship and success.","number":527,"id":"b2:527","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"consumer impulse","meaning":"اندفاع المستهلك","example":"Some students admitted that consumer impulse had once shaped their spending habit more than careful thought.","number":528,"id":"b2:528","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"subtle influence","meaning":"تأثير خفي","example":"A targeted promotion could create demand through subtle influence even when a consumer did not need the item.","number":529,"id":"b2:529","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"advertising strategy","meaning":"استراتيجية إعلانية","example":"Teacher Leila asked whether the advertising strategy genuinely described the product.","number":530,"id":"b2:530","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"misleading","meaning":"إعلان مضلل","example":"But a misleading advertisement may exploit it.","number":531,"id":"b2:531","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"brand loyalty","meaning":"ولاء للعلامة التجارية","example":"They explored brand loyalty, perceived value and the attention economy.","number":532,"id":"b2:532","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"psychological trigger","meaning":"مثير نفسي","example":"A cheerful song created a psychological trigger.","number":533,"id":"b2:533","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"purchase intention","meaning":"نية الشراء","example":"Social proof, such as comments from popular influencers, increased purchase intention.","number":534,"id":"b2:534","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"hidden assumption","meaning":"افتراض خفي","example":"Instead, people should question the hidden assumption behind a message and decide whether the promised benefits are real.","number":535,"id":"b2:535","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"social proof","meaning":"دليل اجتماعي","example":"Social proof, such as comments from popular influencers, increased purchase intention.","number":536,"id":"b2:536","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"personalised content","meaning":"محتوى مخصص","example":"While personalised content made the message seem relevant to each viewer.","number":537,"id":"b2:537","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"attention economy","meaning":"اقتصاد الانتباه","example":"They explored brand loyalty, perceived value and the attention economy.","number":538,"id":"b2:538","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"advertising ethics","meaning":"أخلاقيات الإعلان","example":"Their discussion of advertising ethics and consumer protection led to an interesting conclusion: an informed consumer does not have to reject advertising entirely.","number":539,"id":"b2:539","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"manipulated image","meaning":"صورة معدلة للتأثير","example":"The class noticed a manipulated image and a questionable claim about health.","number":540,"id":"b2:540","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"cognitive shortcut","meaning":"اختصار ذهني","example":"The teacher explained cognitive shortcut.","number":541,"id":"b2:541","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"perceived value","meaning":"قيمة متصورة","example":"They explored brand loyalty, perceived value and the attention economy.","number":542,"id":"b2:542","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"targeted promotion","meaning":"ترويج مستهدف","example":"A targeted promotion could create demand through subtle influence even when a consumer did not need the item.","number":543,"id":"b2:543","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"consumer protection","meaning":"حماية المستهلك","example":"Their discussion of advertising ethics and consumer protection led to an interesting conclusion: an informed consumer does not have to reject advertising entirely.","number":544,"id":"b2:544","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"spending habit","meaning":"عادة إنفاق","example":"Some students admitted that consumer impulse had once shaped their spending habit more than careful thought.","number":545,"id":"b2:545","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"critical awareness","meaning":"وعي نقدي","example":"To practise critical awareness.","number":546,"id":"b2:546","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"commercial message","meaning":"رسالة تجارية","example":"To practise critical awareness, students designed a commercial message that presented accurate information and fair comparisons.","number":547,"id":"b2:547","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"create demand","meaning":"يخلق طلبا","example":"A targeted promotion could create demand through subtle influence even when a consumer did not need the item.","number":548,"id":"b2:548","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"questionable claim","meaning":"ادعاء مشكوك فيه","example":"The class noticed a manipulated image and a questionable claim about health.","number":549,"id":"b2:549","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"},{"term":"informed consumer","meaning":"مستهلك واع","example":"An informed consumer does not have to reject advertising entirely.","number":550,"id":"b2:550","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-22"}],"story":{"title":"The Psychology of Advertising","paragraphs":["During a media lesson, students watched an advertisement for an expensive water bottle. Its persuasive technique was simple: an emotional appeal connected the product with friendship and success. A cheerful song created a psychological trigger, while personalised content made the message seem relevant to each viewer.","Teacher Leila asked whether the advertising strategy genuinely described the product. The class noticed a manipulated image and a questionable claim about health. Social proof, such as comments from popular influencers, increased purchase intention. Some students admitted that consumer impulse had once shaped their spending habit more than careful thought.","They explored brand loyalty, perceived value and the attention economy. A targeted promotion could create demand through subtle influence even when a consumer did not need the item. The teacher explained cognitive shortcut: people often make decisions using quick impressions instead of examining every detail. That shortcut can be useful, but a misleading advertisement may exploit it.","To practise critical awareness, students designed a commercial message that presented accurate information and fair comparisons. Their discussion of advertising ethics and consumer protection led to an interesting conclusion: an informed consumer does not have to reject advertising entirely. Instead, people should question the hidden assumption behind a message and decide whether the promised benefits are real."],"questions":["How did the advertisement connect the bottle with emotions?","What evidence suggested that the advert was misleading?","How might social proof affect purchases?","What habit does the teacher recommend?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-23","title":"The Underground Archive","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 23","level":"B2","set":23,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"classified document","meaning":"وثيقة سرية","example":"An archive inventory mentioned a classified document and coded correspondence, but one missing page had vanished decades earlier.","number":551,"id":"b2:551","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"hidden archive","meaning":"أرشيف مخفي","example":"A historian discovered a hidden archive beneath the town hall.","number":552,"id":"b2:552","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"declassified record","meaning":"سجل رفعت سريته","example":"The historian requested a declassified record and compared it with an official record from the same period.","number":553,"id":"b2:553","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"historical secrecy","meaning":"سرية تاريخية","example":"The mayor worried about historical secrecy and national significance.","number":554,"id":"b2:554","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"coded","meaning":"مراسلات مشفرة","example":"An archive inventory mentioned a classified document and coded correspondence, but one missing page had vanished decades earlier.","number":555,"id":"b2:555","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"official record","meaning":"سجل رسمي","example":"The historian requested a declassified record and compared it with an official record from the same period.","number":556,"id":"b2:556","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"missing page","meaning":"صفحة مفقودة","example":"But one missing page had vanished decades earlier.","number":557,"id":"b2:557","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"restricted access","meaning":"دخول مقيد","example":"The files had restricted access because officials feared the release of sensitive material.","number":558,"id":"b2:558","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"archive inventory","meaning":"جرد الأرشيف","example":"An archive inventory mentioned a classified document and coded correspondence, but one missing page had vanished decades earlier.","number":559,"id":"b2:559","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"disputed account","meaning":"رواية متنازع عليها","example":"A disputed account about a local protest began to look less convincing.","number":560,"id":"b2:560","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"interpret a document","meaning":"يفسر وثيقة","example":"To interpret a document responsibly.","number":561,"id":"b2:561","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"original testimony","meaning":"شهادة أصلية","example":"To interpret a document responsibly, she examined historical context, an authentic signature and the original testimony of people who had lived through the event.","number":562,"id":"b2:562","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"historical context","meaning":"سياق تاريخي","example":"To interpret a document responsibly, she examined historical context, an authentic signature and the original testimony of people who had lived through the event.","number":563,"id":"b2:563","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"institutional memory","meaning":"ذاكرة مؤسسية","example":"The town's institutional memory had therefore grown around an incomplete story.","number":564,"id":"b2:564","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"contradictory report","meaning":"تقرير متناقض","example":"Through the contradictory report.","number":565,"id":"b2:565","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"authentic signature","meaning":"توقيع أصيل","example":"To interpret a document responsibly, she examined historical context, an authentic signature and the original testimony of people who had lived through the event.","number":566,"id":"b2:566","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"uncover a connection","meaning":"يكشف صلة","example":"Through the contradictory report, the historian was able to uncover a connection between the protest and later changes in local law.","number":567,"id":"b2:567","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"public disclosure","meaning":"كشف علني","example":"An investigative scholar offered to help with document preservation and a careful public disclosure of the new evidence.","number":568,"id":"b2:568","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"sensitive material","meaning":"مواد حساسة","example":"The files had restricted access because officials feared the release of sensitive material.","number":569,"id":"b2:569","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"national significance","meaning":"أهمية وطنية","example":"The mayor worried about historical secrecy and national significance.","number":570,"id":"b2:570","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"retrospective","meaning":"تحليل بأثر رجعي","example":"Her retrospective analysis revealed a historical omission.","number":571,"id":"b2:571","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"historical omission","meaning":"إغفال تاريخي","example":"Her retrospective analysis revealed a historical omission.","number":572,"id":"b2:572","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"document","meaning":"صون الوثائق","example":"An investigative scholar offered to help with document preservation and a careful public disclosure of the new evidence.","number":573,"id":"b2:573","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"investigative scholar","meaning":"باحث استقصائي","example":"An investigative scholar offered to help with document preservation and a careful public disclosure of the new evidence.","number":574,"id":"b2:574","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"},{"term":"revealing discovery","meaning":"اكتشاف كاشف","example":"The revealing discovery did not make every witness correct.","number":575,"id":"b2:575","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-23"}],"story":{"title":"The Underground Archive","paragraphs":["A historian discovered a hidden archive beneath the town hall. An archive inventory mentioned a classified document and coded correspondence, but one missing page had vanished decades earlier. The files had restricted access because officials feared the release of sensitive material.","The historian requested a declassified record and compared it with an official record from the same period. Their accounts contradicted one another. To interpret a document responsibly, she examined historical context, an authentic signature and the original testimony of people who had lived through the event. A disputed account about a local protest began to look less convincing.","Her retrospective analysis revealed a historical omission: records of ordinary residents had been deliberately excluded. The town's institutional memory had therefore grown around an incomplete story. An investigative scholar offered to help with document preservation and a careful public disclosure of the new evidence.","The mayor worried about historical secrecy and national significance, but he finally permitted the research. Through the contradictory report, the historian was able to uncover a connection between the protest and later changes in local law. The revealing discovery did not make every witness correct, but it showed why official history needs careful questioning. The historian said that the past becomes more useful when we acknowledge whose voices were missing from it."],"questions":["Why were the archive files difficult to access?","What made the official account less convincing?","What did the historical omission reveal?","What is the main lesson about official history?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-24","title":"The Cultural Exchange Project","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 24","level":"B2","set":24,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"cultural adaptation","meaning":"تكيف ثقافي","example":"The teacher concluded that genuine cultural adaptation is not the ability to imitate every local habit.","number":576,"id":"b2:576","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"stereotype threat","meaning":"تهديد الصور النمطية","example":"One student feared stereotype threat.","number":577,"id":"b2:577","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"intercultural","meaning":"كفاءة التعامل بين الثقافات","example":"The organisers replaced their usual programme with workshops on intercultural competence and cultural sensitivity.","number":578,"id":"b2:578","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"social expectations","meaning":"توقعات اجتماعية","example":"When a group of teenagers arrived from overseas, unfamiliar etiquette and different social expectations created awkward moments.","number":579,"id":"b2:579","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"unfamiliar etiquette","meaning":"آداب غير مألوفة","example":"When a group of teenagers arrived from overseas, unfamiliar etiquette and different social expectations created awkward moments.","number":580,"id":"b2:580","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"social isolation","meaning":"عزلة اجتماعية","example":"Another experienced social isolation because of a language difference.","number":581,"id":"b2:581","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"active listening","meaning":"استماع فعال","example":"They practised active listening and respectful curiosity.","number":582,"id":"b2:582","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"mutual curiosity","meaning":"فضول متبادل","example":"Helping them build mutual curiosity and a sense of belonging.","number":583,"id":"b2:583","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"cultural sensitivity","meaning":"حساسية ثقافية","example":"The organisers replaced their usual programme with workshops on intercultural competence and cultural sensitivity.","number":584,"id":"b2:584","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"sense of belonging","meaning":"إحساس بالانتماء","example":"Helping them build mutual curiosity and a sense of belonging.","number":585,"id":"b2:585","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"preserve identity","meaning":"يحافظ على الهوية","example":"Patience and a willingness to preserve identity while learning from others.","number":586,"id":"b2:586","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"language exchange","meaning":"تبادل لغوي","example":"A language exchange brought students together for a shared experience.","number":587,"id":"b2:587","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"shared experience","meaning":"تجربة مشتركة","example":"A language exchange brought students together for a shared experience, helping them build mutual curiosity and a sense of belonging.","number":588,"id":"b2:588","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"bridge differences","meaning":"يجسر الاختلافات","example":"Their goal was not to erase differences but to bridge differences and find common values.","number":589,"id":"b2:589","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"resolve","meaning":"يحل سوء فهم","example":"The group had to resolve misunderstanding without blaming an entire culture.","number":590,"id":"b2:590","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"cultural assumptions","meaning":"افتراضات ثقافية","example":"One student feared stereotype threat: she worried that a mistake would confirm other people's cultural assumptions.","number":591,"id":"b2:591","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"respectful curiosity","meaning":"فضول محترم","example":"They practised active listening and respectful curiosity.","number":592,"id":"b2:592","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"meaningful","meaning":"تفاعل ذو معنى","example":"They learned that meaningful interaction requires effective communication.","number":593,"id":"b2:593","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"social integration","meaning":"اندماج اجتماعي","example":"As social integration improved.","number":594,"id":"b2:594","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"overcome discomfort","meaning":"يتغلب على عدم الارتياح","example":"Students learned to overcome discomfort.","number":595,"id":"b2:595","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"personal growth","meaning":"نمو شخصي","example":"The programme encouraged personal growth.","number":596,"id":"b2:596","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"cultural diversity","meaning":"تنوع ثقافي","example":"Broaden perspectives and appreciate cultural diversity.","number":597,"id":"b2:597","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"broaden","meaning":"يوسع الآفاق","example":"Broaden perspectives and appreciate cultural diversity.","number":598,"id":"b2:598","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"effective","meaning":"تواصل فعال","example":"They learned that meaningful interaction requires effective communication.","number":599,"id":"b2:599","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"},{"term":"common values","meaning":"قيم مشتركة","example":"Their goal was not to erase differences but to bridge differences and find common values.","number":600,"id":"b2:600","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-24"}],"story":{"title":"The Cultural Exchange Project","paragraphs":["When a group of teenagers arrived from overseas, unfamiliar etiquette and different social expectations created awkward moments. One student feared stereotype threat: she worried that a mistake would confirm other people's cultural assumptions. Another experienced social isolation because of a language difference. The organisers replaced their usual programme with workshops on intercultural competence and cultural sensitivity. Rather than giving long speeches, they practised active listening and respectful curiosity.","A language exchange brought students together for a shared experience, helping them build mutual curiosity and a sense of belonging. During a difficult discussion, one pupil accidentally offended another. The group had to resolve misunderstanding without blaming an entire culture. They learned that meaningful interaction requires effective communication, patience and a willingness to preserve identity while learning from others. Their goal was not to erase differences but to bridge differences and find common values.","As social integration improved, students learned to overcome discomfort, broaden perspectives and appreciate cultural diversity. The programme encouraged personal growth, and many discovered new friendships. The teacher concluded that genuine cultural adaptation is not the ability to imitate every local habit. It is the ability to ask questions kindly, recognise assumptions and meet unfamiliar people as individuals rather than stereotypes."],"questions":["What made some students anxious at first?","Why did organisers emphasise active listening?","How was an accidental offence resolved?","How does the story define genuine cultural adaptation?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-25","title":"The Athlete’s Comeback","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 25","level":"B2","set":25,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"performance setback","meaning":"انتكاسة في الأداء","example":"A serious knee injury created a performance setback for runner Sara.","number":601,"id":"b2:601","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"rehabilitation","meaning":"برنامج تأهيل","example":"Her doctor recommended a rehabilitation programme focused on injury prevention rather than immediate competition.","number":602,"id":"b2:602","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"physical endurance","meaning":"قدرة تحمل بدنية","example":"Sara had always trusted physical endurance.","number":603,"id":"b2:603","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"mental toughness","meaning":"صلابة ذهنية","example":"Sara had always trusted physical endurance, but the experience tested her mental toughness and psychological resilience.","number":604,"id":"b2:604","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"training intensity","meaning":"شدة التدريب","example":"She reduced training intensity and set realistic goals.","number":605,"id":"b2:605","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"injury prevention","meaning":"الوقاية من الإصابات","example":"Her doctor recommended a rehabilitation programme focused on injury prevention rather than immediate competition.","number":606,"id":"b2:606","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"professional","meaning":"إرشاد متخصص","example":"With professional guidance, she reduced training intensity and set realistic goals.","number":607,"id":"b2:607","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"psychological","meaning":"مرونة نفسية","example":"Sara had always trusted physical endurance, but the experience tested her mental toughness and psychological resilience.","number":608,"id":"b2:608","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"athlete's recovery","meaning":"تعافي رياضي","example":"The doctor refused medical clearance until the athlete's recovery was stable.","number":609,"id":"b2:609","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"competitive pressure","meaning":"ضغط المنافسة","example":"Sara faced competitive pressure and career uncertainty.","number":610,"id":"b2:610","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"realistic goals","meaning":"أهداف واقعية","example":"She reduced training intensity and set realistic goals.","number":611,"id":"b2:611","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"gradual","meaning":"تحسن تدريجي","example":"Her coach tracked gradual improvement through performance analysis.","number":612,"id":"b2:612","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"peak condition","meaning":"أفضل حالة بدنية","example":"The long process required self-discipline and personal motivation, especially when social media compared her with athletes already in peak condition.","number":613,"id":"b2:613","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"performance analysis","meaning":"تحليل الأداء","example":"Her coach tracked gradual improvement through performance analysis.","number":614,"id":"b2:614","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"tactical adjustment","meaning":"تعديل تكتيكي","example":"Careful tactical adjustment and regular rest.","number":615,"id":"b2:615","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"team cohesion","meaning":"تماسك الفريق","example":"Her team valued team cohesion more than quick results.","number":616,"id":"b2:616","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"personal motivation","meaning":"دافع شخصي","example":"The long process required self-discipline and personal motivation.","number":617,"id":"b2:617","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"self-discipline","meaning":"انضباط ذاتي","example":"The long process required self-discipline and personal motivation.","number":618,"id":"b2:618","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"medical clearance","meaning":"موافقة طبية للعودة","example":"The doctor refused medical clearance until the athlete's recovery was stable.","number":619,"id":"b2:619","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"career uncertainty","meaning":"عدم يقين مهني","example":"Sara faced competitive pressure and career uncertainty.","number":620,"id":"b2:620","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"overcome adversity","meaning":"يتغلب على المحن","example":"At first Sara called this an unfair delay, but she slowly recognised the need to overcome adversity without ignoring pain.","number":621,"id":"b2:621","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"support network","meaning":"شبكة دعم","example":"So its support network celebrated every training milestone.","number":622,"id":"b2:622","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"training milestone","meaning":"إنجاز تدريبي مرحلي","example":"So its support network celebrated every training milestone.","number":623,"id":"b2:623","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"extraordinary","meaning":"عودة استثنائية","example":"She made an extraordinary comeback at a small community race.","number":624,"id":"b2:624","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"},{"term":"sports psychology","meaning":"علم النفس الرياضي","example":"Her sports psychology teacher explained that success involves more than a stopwatch: protecting long-term wellbeing can require the courage to slow down.","number":625,"id":"b2:625","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-25"}],"story":{"title":"The Athlete’s Comeback","paragraphs":["A serious knee injury created a performance setback for runner Sara. Her doctor recommended a rehabilitation programme focused on injury prevention rather than immediate competition. Sara had always trusted physical endurance, but the experience tested her mental toughness and psychological resilience.","With professional guidance, she reduced training intensity and set realistic goals. Her coach tracked gradual improvement through performance analysis, careful tactical adjustment and regular rest. The long process required self-discipline and personal motivation, especially when social media compared her with athletes already in peak condition.","Sara faced competitive pressure and career uncertainty. Her team valued team cohesion more than quick results, so its support network celebrated every training milestone. The doctor refused medical clearance until the athlete's recovery was stable. At first Sara called this an unfair delay, but she slowly recognised the need to overcome adversity without ignoring pain.","Months later, she made an extraordinary comeback at a small community race. She did not win, yet she felt proud of the progress. Her sports psychology teacher explained that success involves more than a stopwatch: protecting long-term wellbeing can require the courage to slow down. Sara discovered that a comeback is not necessarily a return to exactly the same person. It can be an opportunity to become a wiser one."],"questions":["Why did Sara initially resist the doctor’s advice?","How did the coach measure progress?","Why was medical clearance delayed?","Why was the final race a success despite not winning?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-26","title":"The Wildlife Corridor","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 26","level":"B2","set":26,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"habitat","meaning":"تجزؤ الموطن الطبيعي","example":"A new road divided a forest, causing habitat fragmentation.","number":626,"id":"b2:626","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"wildlife corridor","meaning":"ممر للحياة البرية","example":"A student team proposed a wildlife corridor to restore ecological connectivity and protect species diversity.","number":627,"id":"b2:627","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"ecological balance","meaning":"توازن بيئي","example":"Environmental education helped residents understand the ecological balance.","number":628,"id":"b2:628","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"species diversity","meaning":"تنوع الأنواع","example":"A student team proposed a wildlife corridor to restore ecological connectivity and protect species diversity.","number":629,"id":"b2:629","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"conservation policy","meaning":"سياسة حماية الطبيعة","example":"The town adopted a conservation policy with clear compensation rules.","number":630,"id":"b2:630","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"human","meaning":"زحف بشري على الطبيعة","example":"A rising deforestation rate and human encroachment on the habitat.","number":631,"id":"b2:631","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"deforestation rate","meaning":"معدل إزالة الغابات","example":"A rising deforestation rate and human encroachment on the habitat.","number":632,"id":"b2:632","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"wildlife population","meaning":"أعداد الحيوانات البرية","example":"Rangers feared that the wildlife population would decline because animals could no longer travel between feeding areas.","number":633,"id":"b2:633","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"environmental","meaning":"تقييم بيئي","example":"The project required an environmental assessment.","number":634,"id":"b2:634","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"migration route","meaning":"استعادة مسار الهجرة","example":"They suggested migration route restoration.","number":635,"id":"b2:635","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"biodiversity loss","meaning":"فقدان التنوع الحيوي","example":"Scientists reported biodiversity loss.","number":636,"id":"b2:636","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"protected area","meaning":"منطقة محمية","example":"Protected area boundaries and camera-trap monitoring to track movement.","number":637,"id":"b2:637","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"local opposition","meaning":"معارضة محلية","example":"Farmers expressed local opposition, worrying that land would become unusable.","number":638,"id":"b2:638","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"habitat restoration","meaning":"استعادة الموطن الطبيعي","example":"Students therefore arranged a community partnership, explaining how sustainable land use and habitat restoration could support both farms and wildlife.","number":639,"id":"b2:639","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"conservation funding","meaning":"تمويل الحماية البيئية","example":"Conservation funding was limited.","number":640,"id":"b2:640","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"scientific survey","meaning":"مسح علمي","example":"Their scientific survey also considered survival prospects for an endangered population.","number":641,"id":"b2:641","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"camera-trap","meaning":"رصد بكاميرات خفية","example":"Protected area boundaries and camera-trap monitoring to track movement.","number":642,"id":"b2:642","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"environmental","meaning":"تثقيف بيئي","example":"Environmental education helped residents understand the ecological balance.","number":643,"id":"b2:643","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"community","meaning":"شراكة مجتمعية","example":"Students therefore arranged a community partnership.","number":644,"id":"b2:644","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"survival prospects","meaning":"فرص البقاء","example":"Their scientific survey also considered survival prospects for an endangered population.","number":645,"id":"b2:645","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"sustainable land use","meaning":"استخدام مستدام للأراضي","example":"Students therefore arranged a community partnership, explaining how sustainable land use and habitat restoration could support both farms and wildlife.","number":646,"id":"b2:646","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"ecological","meaning":"ترابط بيئي","example":"A student team proposed a wildlife corridor to restore ecological connectivity and protect species diversity.","number":647,"id":"b2:647","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"endangered","meaning":"مجموعة حيوانية مهددة","example":"Their scientific survey also considered survival prospects for an endangered population.","number":648,"id":"b2:648","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"policy compromise","meaning":"تسوية سياسية","example":"And the council needed a policy compromise.","number":649,"id":"b2:649","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"},{"term":"conservation success","meaning":"نجاح جهود الحماية","example":"While an independent group assessed conservation success.","number":650,"id":"b2:650","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-26"}],"story":{"title":"The Wildlife Corridor","paragraphs":["A new road divided a forest, causing habitat fragmentation. Rangers feared that the wildlife population would decline because animals could no longer travel between feeding areas. A student team proposed a wildlife corridor to restore ecological connectivity and protect species diversity.","The project required an environmental assessment. Scientists reported biodiversity loss, a rising deforestation rate and human encroachment on the habitat. They suggested migration route restoration, protected area boundaries and camera-trap monitoring to track movement. Their scientific survey also considered survival prospects for an endangered population.","Farmers expressed local opposition, worrying that land would become unusable. Conservation funding was limited, and the council needed a policy compromise. Students therefore arranged a community partnership, explaining how sustainable land use and habitat restoration could support both farms and wildlife.","After months of discussion, the town adopted a conservation policy with clear compensation rules. Environmental education helped residents understand the ecological balance, while an independent group assessed conservation success. The first camera images showed animals using the new passage safely. The students learned that ethical wildlife management requires listening to people who live near protected land, not simply drawing boundaries on a map."],"questions":["How did the road threaten wildlife?","Why did farmers initially oppose the corridor?","How did students improve the plan?","What does the case show about conservation?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-27","title":"The Unusual Inheritance","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 27","level":"B2","set":27,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"inheritance dispute","meaning":"نزاع ميراث","example":"An inheritance dispute began immediately.","number":651,"id":"b2:651","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"legal entitlement","meaning":"استحقاق قانوني","example":"With several people questioning legal entitlement and beneficiary rights.","number":652,"id":"b2:652","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"family estate","meaning":"تركة عائلية","example":"Much of the family estate was left to a charitable foundation rather than his relatives.","number":653,"id":"b2:653","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"financial assets","meaning":"أصول مالية","example":"The legal executor asked an independent appraisal company to complete a property valuation and list all financial assets.","number":654,"id":"b2:654","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"tax liability","meaning":"التزام ضريبي","example":"It also found an outstanding debt and possible tax liability.","number":655,"id":"b2:655","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"official will","meaning":"وصية رسمية","example":"When a grandfather died, his family discovered an unusual official will.","number":656,"id":"b2:656","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"legal executor","meaning":"منفذ الوصية قانونيا","example":"The legal executor asked an independent appraisal company to complete a property valuation and list all financial assets.","number":657,"id":"b2:657","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"contested","meaning":"إرث متنازع عليه","example":"One relative demanded legal representation and threatened to challenge the contested inheritance in court.","number":658,"id":"b2:658","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"independent","meaning":"تقييم مستقل","example":"The legal executor asked an independent appraisal company to complete a property valuation and list all financial assets.","number":659,"id":"b2:659","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"property valuation","meaning":"تقييم عقار","example":"The legal executor asked an independent appraisal company to complete a property valuation and list all financial assets.","number":660,"id":"b2:660","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"outstanding debt","meaning":"دين مستحق","example":"It also found an outstanding debt and possible tax liability.","number":661,"id":"b2:661","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"beneficiary rights","meaning":"حقوق المستفيد","example":"With several people questioning legal entitlement and beneficiary rights.","number":662,"id":"b2:662","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"financial advisor","meaning":"مستشار مالي","example":"A financial advisor explained the","number":663,"id":"b2:663","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"risk exposure","meaning":"تعرض للمخاطر","example":"The dispute increased risk exposure for everyone because legal fees might consume the estate.","number":664,"id":"b2:664","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"charitable","meaning":"مؤسسة خيرية","example":"Much of the family estate was left to a charitable foundation rather than his relatives.","number":665,"id":"b2:665","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"ethical obligation","meaning":"واجب أخلاقي","example":"Another argued that the family's personal wealth mattered less than honouring the grandfather's ethical obligation to his community.","number":666,"id":"b2:666","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"settle a dispute","meaning":"يسوي نزاعا","example":"The family agreed to settle a dispute through mediation.","number":667,"id":"b2:667","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"personal wealth","meaning":"ثروة شخصية","example":"Another argued that the family's personal wealth mattered less than honouring the grandfather's ethical obligation to his community.","number":668,"id":"b2:668","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"transparent","meaning":"محاسبة شفافة","example":"A financial advisor explained the inheritance tax rules and the importance of transparent accounting before anyone could discuss equitable distribution.","number":669,"id":"b2:669","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"legal representation","meaning":"تمثيل قانوني","example":"One relative demanded legal representation and threatened to challenge the contested inheritance in court.","number":670,"id":"b2:670","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"inheritance tax","meaning":"ضريبة الميراث","example":"A financial advisor explained the inheritance tax rules and the importance of transparent accounting before anyone could discuss equitable distribution.","number":671,"id":"b2:671","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"financial planning","meaning":"تخطيط مالي","example":"They used financial planning to preserve enough money for urgent family needs while supporting the foundation.","number":672,"id":"b2:672","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"resolve a conflict","meaning":"يحل صراعا","example":"But it helped resolve a conflict without destroying relationships.","number":673,"id":"b2:673","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"long-term legacy","meaning":"إرث طويل الأمد","example":"The youngest granddaughter said the most valuable long-term legacy was not a particular building or bank account.","number":674,"id":"b2:674","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"},{"term":"equitable","meaning":"توزيع عادل","example":"A financial advisor explained the inheritance tax rules and the importance of transparent accounting before anyone could discuss equitable distribution.","number":675,"id":"b2:675","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-27"}],"story":{"title":"The Unusual Inheritance","paragraphs":["When a grandfather died, his family discovered an unusual official will. Much of the family estate was left to a charitable foundation rather than his relatives. An inheritance dispute began immediately, with several people questioning legal entitlement and beneficiary rights.","The legal executor asked an independent appraisal company to complete a property valuation and list all financial assets. It also found an outstanding debt and possible tax liability. A financial advisor explained the inheritance tax rules and the importance of transparent accounting before anyone could discuss equitable distribution.","One relative demanded legal representation and threatened to challenge the contested inheritance in court. Another argued that the family's personal wealth mattered less than honouring the grandfather's ethical obligation to his community. The dispute increased risk exposure for everyone because legal fees might consume the estate.","The family agreed to settle a dispute through mediation. They used financial planning to preserve enough money for urgent family needs while supporting the foundation. This compromise did not give everyone exactly what they wanted, but it helped resolve a conflict without destroying relationships. The youngest granddaughter said the most valuable long-term legacy was not a particular building or bank account. It was the example of generosity and thoughtful responsibility that the family might choose to continue."],"questions":["Why did the family disagree over the will?","Why was independent valuation important?","What danger did a legal battle create?","What does the granddaughter mean by long-term legacy?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-28","title":"The Drone Rescue","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 28","level":"B2","set":28,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"aerial mapping","meaning":"رسم خرائط جوية","example":"Its remote pilot planned aerial mapping and a search radius based on the last known location.","number":676,"id":"b2:676","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"unmanned aircraft","meaning":"طائرة من دون طيار","example":"A volunteer team began rescue coordination using an unmanned aircraft.","number":677,"id":"b2:677","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"remote pilot","meaning":"طيار عن بعد","example":"Its remote pilot planned aerial mapping and a search radius based on the last known location.","number":678,"id":"b2:678","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"real-time footage","meaning":"تصوير لحظي","example":"Real-time footage revealed a weak heat signal near a rock shelter.","number":679,"id":"b2:679","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"rescue coordination","meaning":"تنسيق الإنقاذ","example":"A volunteer team began rescue coordination using an unmanned aircraft.","number":680,"id":"b2:680","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"emergency","meaning":"نشر عاجل للمعدات","example":"During a mountain storm, a missing hiker sent one emergency message before losing contact.","number":681,"id":"b2:681","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"battery limitation","meaning":"قيد سعة البطارية","example":"Battery limitation and signal interference complicated the urgent mission.","number":682,"id":"b2:682","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"obstacle detection","meaning":"اكتشاف العوائق","example":"The drone carried a thermal camera and obstacle detection software.","number":683,"id":"b2:683","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"thermal camera","meaning":"كاميرا حرارية","example":"The drone carried a thermal camera and obstacle detection software.","number":684,"id":"b2:684","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"missing hiker","meaning":"متنزه مفقود","example":"A missing hiker sent one emergency message before losing contact.","number":685,"id":"b2:685","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"search radius","meaning":"نطاق البحث","example":"Its remote pilot planned aerial mapping and a search radius based on the last known location.","number":686,"id":"b2:686","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"rescue priority","meaning":"أولوية الإنقاذ","example":"The field command officer balanced rescue priority with the safety of everyone involved.","number":687,"id":"b2:687","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"terrain analysis","meaning":"تحليل التضاريس","example":"The pilot used terrain analysis to","number":688,"id":"b2:688","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"signal interference","meaning":"تشويش الإشارة","example":"Battery limitation and signal interference complicated the urgent mission.","number":689,"id":"b2:689","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"autonomous","meaning":"ملاحة ذاتية","example":"When autonomous navigation failed, the team switched to manual control.","number":690,"id":"b2:690","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"flight restriction","meaning":"قيد طيران","example":"The pilot used terrain analysis to select a safe route, while the airspace authority confirmed a temporary flight restriction for other aircraft.","number":691,"id":"b2:691","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"airspace authority","meaning":"جهة تنظيم المجال الجوي","example":"The pilot used terrain analysis to select a safe route, while the airspace authority confirmed a temporary flight restriction for other aircraft.","number":692,"id":"b2:692","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"urgent mission","meaning":"مهمة عاجلة","example":"Battery limitation and signal interference complicated the urgent mission.","number":693,"id":"b2:693","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"rescue efficiency","meaning":"كفاءة الإنقاذ","example":"Their new technology improved rescue efficiency.","number":694,"id":"b2:694","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"operational risk","meaning":"مخاطر تشغيلية","example":"But this was a real operational risk.","number":695,"id":"b2:695","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"technical failure","meaning":"عطل تقني","example":"They had practised a backup strategy for technical failure.","number":696,"id":"b2:696","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"backup strategy","meaning":"استراتيجية احتياطية","example":"They had practised a backup strategy for technical failure.","number":697,"id":"b2:697","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"life-saving","meaning":"معدات منقذة للحياة","example":"The team used life-saving equipment to locate survivors and began emergency deployment of medical supplies.","number":698,"id":"b2:698","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"locate survivors","meaning":"يعثر على الناجين","example":"The team used life-saving equipment to locate survivors and began emergency deployment of medical supplies.","number":699,"id":"b2:699","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"},{"term":"field command","meaning":"قيادة ميدانية","example":"The field command officer balanced rescue priority with the safety of everyone involved.","number":700,"id":"b2:700","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-28"}],"story":{"title":"The Drone Rescue","paragraphs":["During a mountain storm, a missing hiker sent one emergency message before losing contact. A volunteer team began rescue coordination using an unmanned aircraft. Its remote pilot planned aerial mapping and a search radius based on the last known location.","The drone carried a thermal camera and obstacle detection software, which helped reveal movement through fog. However, battery limitation and signal interference complicated the urgent mission. The pilot used terrain analysis to select a safe route, while the airspace authority confirmed a temporary flight restriction for other aircraft.","When autonomous navigation failed, the team switched to manual control. They had practised a backup strategy for technical failure, but this was a real operational risk. The field command officer balanced rescue priority with the safety of everyone involved. Real-time footage revealed a weak heat signal near a rock shelter.","The team used life-saving equipment to locate survivors and began emergency deployment of medical supplies. Their new technology improved rescue efficiency, yet the officer insisted that human judgement remained essential. The successful operation reminded students that advanced tools work best when trained people understand their limitations and make careful decisions under pressure."],"questions":["Which drone features helped locate the hiker?","What problems limited the drone?","Why was human judgement still important?","What is the central lesson about technology?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-29","title":"The Language of Silence","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 29","level":"B2","set":29,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"nonverbal","meaning":"تواصل غير لفظي","example":"At a new school, Sami often misunderstood nonverbal communication.","number":701,"id":"b2:701","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"body language","meaning":"لغة الجسد","example":"His teacher explained that body language may reflect a hidden emotion.","number":702,"id":"b2:702","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"hidden emotion","meaning":"عاطفة خفية","example":"His teacher explained that body language may reflect a hidden emotion.","number":703,"id":"b2:703","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"subtle gesture","meaning":"إيماءة دقيقة","example":"A subtle gesture can convey an unintended message.","number":704,"id":"b2:704","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"unintended message","meaning":"رسالة غير مقصودة","example":"A subtle gesture can convey an unintended message.","number":705,"id":"b2:705","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"emotional","meaning":"ذكاء عاطفي","example":"The class explored emotional intelligence.","number":706,"id":"b2:706","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"interpret silence","meaning":"يفسر الصمت","example":"Social cue recognition and the challenge of learning to interpret silence.","number":707,"id":"b2:707","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"interpersonal tension","meaning":"توتر بين الأشخاص","example":"Their interpersonal tension grew until a counsellor encouraged an empathic response.","number":708,"id":"b2:708","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"empathic response","meaning":"استجابة متعاطفة","example":"Their interpersonal tension grew until a counsellor encouraged an empathic response.","number":709,"id":"b2:709","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"active observation","meaning":"ملاحظة نشطة","example":"The teacher asked students to practise active observation and reflective listening before drawing conclusions about anyone's personal boundary or social intentions.","number":710,"id":"b2:710","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"personal boundary","meaning":"حد شخصي","example":"The teacher asked students to practise active observation and reflective listening before drawing conclusions about anyone's personal boundary or social intentions.","number":711,"id":"b2:711","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"build rapport","meaning":"يبني ألفة","example":"Sami tried to build rapport with the classmate.","number":712,"id":"b2:712","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"emotional awareness","meaning":"وعي عاطفي","example":"Sami showed emotional awareness and","number":713,"id":"b2:713","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"respectful distance","meaning":"مسافة محترمة","example":"But he misread intentions again when she requested respectful distance.","number":714,"id":"b2:714","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"social cue","meaning":"إشارة اجتماعية","example":"Social cue recognition and the challenge of learning to interpret silence.","number":715,"id":"b2:715","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"misread intentions","meaning":"يسيء فهم النوايا","example":"But he misread intentions again when she requested respectful distance.","number":716,"id":"b2:716","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"genuine connection","meaning":"صلة صادقة","example":"This honest question replaced an unspoken assumption with a genuine connection.","number":717,"id":"b2:717","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"conflict resolution","meaning":"حل النزاعات","example":"Their conflict resolution did not require constant conversation.","number":718,"id":"b2:718","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"unspoken","meaning":"افتراض غير معلن","example":"This honest question replaced an unspoken assumption with a genuine connection.","number":719,"id":"b2:719","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"reflective listening","meaning":"استماع تأملي","example":"The teacher asked students to practise active observation and reflective listening before drawing conclusions about anyone's personal boundary or social intentions.","number":720,"id":"b2:720","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"communicate","meaning":"يظهر التعاطف","example":"They began to communicate empathy through small acts of mutual support.","number":721,"id":"b2:721","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"emotional","meaning":"هشاشة عاطفية","example":"Sami showed emotional awareness and recognised her emotional vulnerability.","number":722,"id":"b2:722","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"thoughtful response","meaning":"استجابة مدروسة","example":"One thoughtful response was simply to ask whether she wanted to talk.","number":723,"id":"b2:723","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"mutual support","meaning":"دعم متبادل","example":"They began to communicate empathy through small acts of mutual support.","number":724,"id":"b2:724","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"},{"term":"lasting trust","meaning":"ثقة دائمة","example":"Over time, lasting trust developed because both students listened carefully and accepted that other people might express feelings in ways they had not expected.","number":725,"id":"b2:725","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-29"}],"story":{"title":"The Language of Silence","paragraphs":["At a new school, Sami often misunderstood nonverbal communication. A classmate's folded arms appeared hostile, so he assumed she disliked him. His teacher explained that body language may reflect a hidden emotion, not a clear opinion about another person.","The class explored emotional intelligence, social cue recognition and the challenge of learning to interpret silence. A subtle gesture can convey an unintended message. The teacher asked students to practise active observation and reflective listening before drawing conclusions about anyone's personal boundary or social intentions.","Sami tried to build rapport with the classmate, but he misread intentions again when she requested respectful distance. Their interpersonal tension grew until a counsellor encouraged an empathic response. Rather than demanding an explanation, Sami showed emotional awareness and recognised her emotional vulnerability.","They began to communicate empathy through small acts of mutual support. One thoughtful response was simply to ask whether she wanted to talk. This honest question replaced an unspoken assumption with a genuine connection. Their conflict resolution did not require constant conversation; sometimes respecting silence was equally valuable. Over time, lasting trust developed because both students listened carefully and accepted that other people might express feelings in ways they had not expected."],"questions":["Why did Sami misinterpret his classmate’s folded arms?","What did the teacher say about nonverbal communication?","How did Sami begin to rebuild trust?","What does the story suggest about empathy?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-30","title":"The Museum Restitution","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 30","level":"B2","set":30,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"cultural restitution","meaning":"إعادة ممتلكات ثقافية","example":"The case became a public test of cultural restitution.","number":726,"id":"b2:726","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"contested artefact","meaning":"قطعة أثرية محل نزاع","example":"A museum received a restitution claim from an overseas community seeking the return of a contested artefact.","number":727,"id":"b2:727","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"historical ownership","meaning":"ملكية تاريخية","example":"Making historical ownership difficult to establish.","number":728,"id":"b2:728","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"colonial legacy","meaning":"إرث استعماري","example":"The object had entered the museum collection during a period of colonial legacy, making historical ownership difficult to establish.","number":729,"id":"b2:729","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"provenance research","meaning":"بحث في أصل المقتنيات","example":"Provenance research raised questions about ethical acquisition and possible historical injustice.","number":730,"id":"b2:730","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"ethical acquisition","meaning":"اقتناء أخلاقي","example":"Provenance research raised questions about ethical acquisition and possible historical injustice.","number":731,"id":"b2:731","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"restitution claim","meaning":"مطالبة باسترداد","example":"A museum received a restitution claim from an overseas community seeking the return of a contested artefact.","number":732,"id":"b2:732","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"diplomatic discussion","meaning":"نقاش دبلوماسي","example":"An independent commission examined disputed evidence and proposed a diplomatic discussion with community representatives.","number":733,"id":"b2:733","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"museum collection","meaning":"مجموعة متحفية","example":"The object had entered the museum collection during a period of colonial legacy, making historical ownership difficult to establish.","number":734,"id":"b2:734","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"repatriation","meaning":"اتفاق إعادة إلى الوطن","example":"Eventually, a repatriation agreement was reached with plans for educational cooperation.","number":735,"id":"b2:735","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"cultural significance","meaning":"أهمية ثقافية","example":"A scholarly debate considered cultural significance.","number":736,"id":"b2:736","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"original community","meaning":"المجتمع الأصلي","example":"A scholarly debate considered cultural significance, the wishes of the original community and the need for cultural heritage protection.","number":737,"id":"b2:737","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"historical injustice","meaning":"ظلم تاريخي","example":"Provenance research raised questions about ethical acquisition and possible historical injustice.","number":738,"id":"b2:738","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"legal ownership","meaning":"ملكية قانونية","example":"The museum director insisted that legal ownership was clear.","number":739,"id":"b2:739","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"moral responsibility","meaning":"مسؤولية أخلاقية","example":"The museum director insisted that legal ownership was clear, but students argued that moral responsibility might require more than following the law.","number":740,"id":"b2:740","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"independent","meaning":"لجنة مستقلة","example":"An independent commission examined disputed evidence and proposed a diplomatic discussion with community representatives.","number":741,"id":"b2:741","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"disputed evidence","meaning":"أدلة محل خلاف","example":"An independent commission examined disputed evidence and proposed a diplomatic discussion with community representatives.","number":742,"id":"b2:742","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"cultural heritage","meaning":"حماية التراث الثقافي","example":"A scholarly debate considered cultural significance, the wishes of the original community and the need for cultural heritage protection.","number":743,"id":"b2:743","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"loan arrangement","meaning":"ترتيب إعارة","example":"Including a loan arrangement.","number":744,"id":"b2:744","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"public exhibition","meaning":"حقوق العرض العام","example":"Shared stewardship and public exhibition rights.","number":745,"id":"b2:745","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"scholarly debate","meaning":"نقاش أكاديمي","example":"A scholarly debate considered cultural significance.","number":746,"id":"b2:746","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"shared stewardship","meaning":"رعاية مشتركة","example":"Shared stewardship and public exhibition rights.","number":747,"id":"b2:747","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"historic apology","meaning":"اعتذار تاريخي","example":"The director offered a historic apology for the institution's past silence.","number":748,"id":"b2:748","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"healing process","meaning":"عملية تعاف معنوي","example":"Yet many participants described it as a healing process.","number":749,"id":"b2:749","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"},{"term":"meaningful","meaning":"استرداد ذو معنى","example":"The students learned that meaningful restitution is not just the movement of an object from one building to another.","number":750,"id":"b2:750","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-30"}],"story":{"title":"The Museum Restitution","paragraphs":["A museum received a restitution claim from an overseas community seeking the return of a contested artefact. The object had entered the museum collection during a period of colonial legacy, making historical ownership difficult to establish. Provenance research raised questions about ethical acquisition and possible historical injustice.","The museum director insisted that legal ownership was clear, but students argued that moral responsibility might require more than following the law. A scholarly debate considered cultural significance, the wishes of the original community and the need for cultural heritage protection. The case became a public test of cultural restitution.","An independent commission examined disputed evidence and proposed a diplomatic discussion with community representatives. Several options were explored, including a loan arrangement, shared stewardship and public exhibition rights. Eventually, a repatriation agreement was reached with plans for educational cooperation.","At the handover, the director offered a historic apology for the institution's past silence. The process could not undo every harm, yet many participants described it as a healing process. The students learned that meaningful restitution is not just the movement of an object from one building to another. It is a chance to reconsider whose history is being told, who has the right to tell it and what fairness demands today."],"questions":["Why was legal ownership not the only issue?","What did the independent commission contribute?","Why did the museum apologise?","What makes restitution meaningful beyond moving an object?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-31","title":"The Future Classroom","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 31","level":"B2","set":31,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"adaptive learning","meaning":"تعلم تكيفي","example":"A school introduced adaptive learning software that offered each pupil a personalised curriculum.","number":751,"id":"b2:751","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"personalised","meaning":"منهج مخصص","example":"A school introduced adaptive learning software that offered each pupil a personalised curriculum.","number":752,"id":"b2:752","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"digital divide","meaning":"فجوة رقمية","example":"One teacher noticed a digital divide.","number":753,"id":"b2:753","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"formative","meaning":"تقييم تكويني","example":"The teacher used formative assessment and meaningful feedback rather than relying on a single score.","number":754,"id":"b2:754","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"critical literacy","meaning":"ثقافة نقدية","example":"The class explored critical literacy.","number":755,"id":"b2:755","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"student agency","meaning":"فاعلية الطالب في اختياراته","example":"Her students also wanted student agency.","number":756,"id":"b2:756","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"inclusive pedagogy","meaning":"تعليم شامل للجميع","example":"She proposed inclusive pedagogy and accessible materials so everyone could participate.","number":757,"id":"b2:757","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"blended learning","meaning":"تعلم مدمج","example":"Its designers argued that blended learning could improve the learning outcome for students who needed extra help.","number":758,"id":"b2:758","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"lifelong learning","meaning":"تعلم مدى الحياة","example":"Students prepared posters about lifelong learning and the ability to continue growing beyond school.","number":759,"id":"b2:759","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"skill gap","meaning":"فجوة مهارات","example":"The system risked widening the skill gap and undermining educational equity.","number":760,"id":"b2:760","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"educational equity","meaning":"إنصاف تعليمي","example":"The system risked widening the skill gap and undermining educational equity.","number":761,"id":"b2:761","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"cognitive","meaning":"نمو إدراكي","example":"Cognitive development and the importance of emotional wellbeing.","number":762,"id":"b2:762","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"learning outcome","meaning":"نتاج تعلم","example":"Its designers argued that blended learning could improve the learning outcome for students who needed extra help.","number":763,"id":"b2:763","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"evidence-informed","meaning":"تدريس مستند للأدلة","example":"She believed evidence-informed teaching should respect teacher autonomy and encourage collaborative inquiry.","number":764,"id":"b2:764","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"collaborative inquiry","meaning":"استقصاء تعاوني","example":"She believed evidence-informed teaching should respect teacher autonomy and encourage collaborative inquiry.","number":765,"id":"b2:765","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"teacher autonomy","meaning":"استقلالية المعلم","example":"She believed evidence-informed teaching should respect teacher autonomy and encourage collaborative inquiry.","number":766,"id":"b2:766","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"algorithmic","meaning":"توصية خوارزمية","example":"The programme promised measurable progress using learning analytics and algorithmic recommendation.","number":767,"id":"b2:767","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"meaningful feedback","meaning":"تغذية راجعة مفيدة","example":"The teacher used formative assessment and meaningful feedback rather than relying on a single score.","number":768,"id":"b2:768","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"emotional wellbeing","meaning":"رفاه نفسي","example":"Cognitive development and the importance of emotional wellbeing.","number":769,"id":"b2:769","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"learning analytics","meaning":"تحليلات التعلم","example":"The programme promised measurable progress using learning analytics and algorithmic recommendation.","number":770,"id":"b2:770","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"digital citizenship","meaning":"مواطنة رقمية","example":"Technology could still support creative problem-solving and digital citizenship, but it would not replace discussion, curiosity or human-centred education.","number":771,"id":"b2:771","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"measurable progress","meaning":"تقدم قابل للقياس","example":"The programme promised measurable progress using learning analytics and algorithmic recommendation.","number":772,"id":"b2:772","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"creative","meaning":"حل مبتكر للمشكلات","example":"Technology could still support creative problem-solving and digital citizenship, but it would not replace discussion, curiosity or human-centred education.","number":773,"id":"b2:773","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"accessible materials","meaning":"مواد يسهل الوصول إليها","example":"She proposed inclusive pedagogy and accessible materials so everyone could participate.","number":774,"id":"b2:774","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"},{"term":"human-centred","meaning":"تعليم يركز على الإنسان","example":"Curiosity or human-centred education.","number":775,"id":"b2:775","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-31"}],"story":{"title":"The Future Classroom","paragraphs":["A school introduced adaptive learning software that offered each pupil a personalised curriculum. The programme promised measurable progress using learning analytics and algorithmic recommendation. Its designers argued that blended learning could improve the learning outcome for students who needed extra help.","However, one teacher noticed a digital divide: some families had little internet access. The system risked widening the skill gap and undermining educational equity. She proposed inclusive pedagogy and accessible materials so everyone could participate. Her students also wanted student agency, meaning a voice in how they learned.","During a workshop, the class explored critical literacy, cognitive development and the importance of emotional wellbeing. The teacher used formative assessment and meaningful feedback rather than relying on a single score. She believed evidence-informed teaching should respect teacher autonomy and encourage collaborative inquiry.","The school adjusted its programme. Technology could still support creative problem-solving and digital citizenship, but it would not replace discussion, curiosity or human-centred education. Students prepared posters about lifelong learning and the ability to continue growing beyond school. The headteacher admitted that the future classroom should not simply contain more devices. It should create better opportunities for every learner to think deeply, ask questions and take responsibility for progress."],"questions":["What problem did the teacher identify in the new system?","How did she make assessment more balanced?","Why did students want agency?","How does the story define a successful future classroom?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-32","title":"The Impossible Expedition","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 32","level":"B2","set":32,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"uncharted territory","meaning":"منطقة غير مستكشفة","example":"An exploration team entered uncharted territory beyond a high mountain pass.","number":776,"id":"b2:776","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"hostile terrain","meaning":"تضاريس وعرة خطرة","example":"The hostile terrain and extreme altitude created a logistical challenge before they had even reached the main ridge.","number":777,"id":"b2:777","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"extreme altitude","meaning":"ارتفاع شاهق","example":"The hostile terrain and extreme altitude created a logistical challenge before they had even reached the main ridge.","number":778,"id":"b2:778","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"logistical challenge","meaning":"تحد لوجستي","example":"The hostile terrain and extreme altitude created a logistical challenge before they had even reached the main ridge.","number":779,"id":"b2:779","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"survival instinct","meaning":"غريزة البقاء","example":"Physical exhaustion and environmental exposure weakened their survival instinct, while a morale collapse threatened cooperation.","number":780,"id":"b2:780","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"unexpected obstacle","meaning":"عائق غير متوقع","example":"The team encountered an unexpected obstacle.","number":781,"id":"b2:781","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"dangerous crossing","meaning":"عبور خطير","example":"Their leader planned a dangerous crossing using limited provisions.","number":782,"id":"b2:782","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"navigation error","meaning":"خطأ ملاحي","example":"After a navigation error, the team encountered an unexpected obstacle: a narrow bridge had collapsed.","number":783,"id":"b2:783","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"limited provisions","meaning":"مؤن محدودة","example":"Their leader planned a dangerous crossing using limited provisions.","number":784,"id":"b2:784","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"shifting weather","meaning":"طقس متقلب","example":"But shifting weather made every decision uncertain.","number":785,"id":"b2:785","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"physical exhaustion","meaning":"إنهاك جسدي","example":"Physical exhaustion and environmental exposure weakened their survival instinct, while a morale collapse threatened cooperation.","number":786,"id":"b2:786","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"strategic retreat","meaning":"انسحاب استراتيجي","example":"She chose a strategic retreat rather than gambling with lives.","number":787,"id":"b2:787","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"leadership under","meaning":"قيادة تحت الضغط","example":"Her leadership under pressure","number":788,"id":"b2:788","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"mutual reliance","meaning":"اعتماد متبادل","example":"Through mutual reliance, the explorers created an improvised solution to cross a safer valley and sent an emergency signal from an open area.","number":789,"id":"b2:789","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"calculated risk","meaning":"مخاطرة محسوبة","example":"Her leadership under pressure required critical judgement and a calculated risk.","number":790,"id":"b2:790","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"extraordinary","meaning":"إصرار استثنائي","example":"Their extraordinary determination helped them reach a rescue point.","number":791,"id":"b2:791","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"decisive moment","meaning":"لحظة حاسمة","example":"The leader faced a decisive moment.","number":792,"id":"b2:792","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"emergency signal","meaning":"إشارة استغاثة","example":"Through mutual reliance, the explorers created an improvised solution to cross a safer valley and sent an emergency signal from an open area.","number":793,"id":"b2:793","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"morale collapse","meaning":"انهيار المعنويات","example":"While a morale collapse threatened cooperation.","number":794,"id":"b2:794","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"critical judgement","meaning":"حكم بالغ الأهمية","example":"Her leadership under pressure required critical judgement and a calculated risk.","number":795,"id":"b2:795","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"improvised solution","meaning":"حل مرتجل","example":"Through mutual reliance, the explorers created an improvised solution to cross a safer valley and sent an emergency signal from an open area.","number":796,"id":"b2:796","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"breathtaking view","meaning":"منظر يحبس الأنفاس","example":"As the helicopter lifted above the breathtaking view.","number":797,"id":"b2:797","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"environmental","meaning":"تعرض للعوامل الطبيعية","example":"Physical exhaustion and environmental exposure weakened their survival instinct, while a morale collapse threatened cooperation.","number":798,"id":"b2:798","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"successful","meaning":"إخلاء ناجح","example":"A successful evacuation ended the mission.","number":799,"id":"b2:799","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"},{"term":"lessons learned","meaning":"دروس مستفادة","example":"The leader discussed the lessons learned.","number":800,"id":"b2:800","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-32"}],"story":{"title":"The Impossible Expedition","paragraphs":["An exploration team entered uncharted territory beyond a high mountain pass. The hostile terrain and extreme altitude created a logistical challenge before they had even reached the main ridge. Their leader planned a dangerous crossing using limited provisions, but shifting weather made every decision uncertain.","After a navigation error, the team encountered an unexpected obstacle: a narrow bridge had collapsed. Physical exhaustion and environmental exposure weakened their survival instinct, while a morale collapse threatened cooperation. Some climbers insisted on continuing, calling retreat a failure.","The leader faced a decisive moment. Her leadership under pressure required critical judgement and a calculated risk. She chose a strategic retreat rather than gambling with lives. Through mutual reliance, the explorers created an improvised solution to cross a safer valley and sent an emergency signal from an open area.","Their extraordinary determination helped them reach a rescue point. A successful evacuation ended the mission, though the famous peak remained unconquered. As the helicopter lifted above the breathtaking view, the leader discussed the lessons learned. True courage, she said, is not the refusal to turn back. It is the willingness to revise a plan when the evidence shows that pride has become more dangerous than the mountain."],"questions":["What dangers combined to threaten the expedition?","Why did the leader order a retreat?","What helped the team reach safety?","Why is retreat presented as courageous?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-33","title":"The Startup That Saved Water","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 33","level":"B2","set":33,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"water scarcity","meaning":"ندرة المياه","example":"In a village struggling with water scarcity.","number":801,"id":"b2:801","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"water purification","meaning":"تنقية المياه","example":"In a village struggling with water scarcity, students designed a water purification device using a simple filtration system.","number":802,"id":"b2:802","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"filtration system","meaning":"نظام ترشيح","example":"In a village struggling with water scarcity, students designed a water purification device using a simple filtration system.","number":803,"id":"b2:803","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"technical prototype","meaning":"نموذج تقني أولي","example":"Their technical prototype worked.","number":804,"id":"b2:804","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"innovation grant","meaning":"منحة ابتكار","example":"Their technical prototype worked, but the team needed an innovation grant to test it outside the school laboratory.","number":805,"id":"b2:805","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"social enterprise","meaning":"مشروع اجتماعي","example":"They created a social enterprise rather than an ordinary commercial company.","number":806,"id":"b2:806","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"responsible","meaning":"استثمار مسؤول","example":"An investor recognised its commercial potential and offered responsible investment, but demanded rapid market expansion.","number":807,"id":"b2:807","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"commercial potential","meaning":"إمكانات تجارية","example":"An investor recognised its commercial potential and offered responsible investment, but demanded rapid market expansion.","number":808,"id":"b2:808","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"affordable solution","meaning":"حل ميسور التكلفة","example":"Their pilot programme needed community feedback and an affordable solution that families could repair locally.","number":809,"id":"b2:809","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"rural households","meaning":"أسر ريفية","example":"The students worried about an investment dilemma: growing too quickly might raise maintenance costs and make the product unaffordable for rural households.","number":810,"id":"b2:810","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"pilot programme","meaning":"برنامج تجريبي","example":"Their pilot programme needed community feedback and an affordable solution that families could repair locally.","number":811,"id":"b2:811","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"cost reduction","meaning":"خفض التكاليف","example":"While cost reduction made long-term adoption more realistic.","number":812,"id":"b2:812","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"community feedback","meaning":"ملاحظات المجتمع","example":"Their pilot programme needed community feedback and an affordable solution that families could repair locally.","number":813,"id":"b2:813","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"measurable impact","meaning":"أثر قابل للقياس","example":"They measured the project's success through measurable impact rather than short-term sales alone.","number":814,"id":"b2:814","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"ethical enterprise","meaning":"مؤسسة أخلاقية","example":"They needed scalable technology without abandoning the principles of an ethical enterprise.","number":815,"id":"b2:815","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"distribution network","meaning":"شبكة توزيع","example":"The team redesigned the device using user-centred design and improved the distribution network.","number":816,"id":"b2:816","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"scalable technology","meaning":"تقنية قابلة للتوسع","example":"They needed scalable technology without abandoning the principles of an ethical enterprise.","number":817,"id":"b2:817","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"maintenance costs","meaning":"تكاليف الصيانة","example":"The students worried about an investment dilemma: growing too quickly might raise maintenance costs and make the product unaffordable for rural households.","number":818,"id":"b2:818","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"user-centred design","meaning":"تصميم يركز على المستخدم","example":"The team redesigned the device using user-centred design and improved the distribution network.","number":819,"id":"b2:819","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"sustainability","meaning":"تحدي استدامة","example":"As demand increased, the team faced a sustainability challenge.","number":820,"id":"b2:820","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"long-term adoption","meaning":"اعتماد طويل الأمد","example":"While cost reduction made long-term adoption more realistic.","number":821,"id":"b2:821","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"local ownership","meaning":"ملكية محلية","example":"Local ownership would help the village maintain it.","number":822,"id":"b2:822","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"investment dilemma","meaning":"معضلة استثمار","example":"The students worried about an investment dilemma.","number":823,"id":"b2:823","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"breakthrough device","meaning":"جهاز مبتكر رائد","example":"The breakthrough device eventually reached nearby villages.","number":824,"id":"b2:824","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"},{"term":"market expansion","meaning":"توسع السوق","example":"But demanded rapid market expansion.","number":825,"id":"b2:825","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-33"}],"story":{"title":"The Startup That Saved Water","paragraphs":["In a village struggling with water scarcity, students designed a water purification device using a simple filtration system. Their technical prototype worked, but the team needed an innovation grant to test it outside the school laboratory. They created a social enterprise rather than an ordinary commercial company.","An investor recognised its commercial potential and offered responsible investment, but demanded rapid market expansion. The students worried about an investment dilemma: growing too quickly might raise maintenance costs and make the product unaffordable for rural households. Their pilot programme needed community feedback and an affordable solution that families could repair locally.","The team redesigned the device using user-centred design and improved the distribution network. Local ownership would help the village maintain it, while cost reduction made long-term adoption more realistic. They measured the project's success through measurable impact rather than short-term sales alone.","As demand increased, the team faced a sustainability challenge. They needed scalable technology without abandoning the principles of an ethical enterprise. The breakthrough device eventually reached nearby villages, and reliable water became easier to obtain. Their teacher said that innovation is strongest when the people who use a product can also understand, maintain and benefit from it."],"questions":["What problem did the first prototype address?","Why was rapid expansion risky?","How did community feedback influence the design?","How did the team define success?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-34","title":"The Research Integrity Case","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 34","level":"B2","set":34,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"academic misconduct","meaning":"سوء سلوك أكاديمي","example":"Some colleagues suspected data manipulation and an academic misconduct scandal.","number":826,"id":"b2:826","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"plagiarism","meaning":"اتهام بالسرقة الأدبية","example":"Others warned against a plagiarism accusation without proof.","number":827,"id":"b2:827","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"peer review","meaning":"تحكيم الأقران","example":"During peer review of a follow-up paper.","number":828,"id":"b2:828","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"research","meaning":"منهجية البحث","example":"She asked her research supervisor to organise an evidence review before making public claims.","number":829,"id":"b2:829","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"reproducible result","meaning":"نتيجة قابلة لإعادة الإنتاج","example":"Maya understood that statistical significance depends on appropriate methods and a reproducible result.","number":830,"id":"b2:830","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"flawed experiment","meaning":"تجربة معيبة","example":"Graduate student Maya noticed a flawed experiment.","number":831,"id":"b2:831","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"selective reporting","meaning":"عرض انتقائي للنتائج","example":"And several graphs suggested selective reporting.","number":832,"id":"b2:832","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"statistical","meaning":"دلالة إحصائية","example":"Maya understood that statistical significance depends on appropriate methods and a reproducible result.","number":833,"id":"b2:833","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"data manipulation","meaning":"تلاعب بالبيانات","example":"Some colleagues suspected data manipulation and an academic misconduct scandal.","number":834,"id":"b2:834","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"academic reputation","meaning":"سمعة أكاديمية","example":"They also discussed professional consequences and academic reputation.","number":835,"id":"b2:835","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"conflict disclosure","meaning":"إفصاح عن تضارب المصالح","example":"Conflict disclosure and the pressure of publish or perish.","number":836,"id":"b2:836","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"research supervisor","meaning":"مشرف بحثي","example":"She asked her research supervisor to organise an evidence review before making public claims.","number":837,"id":"b2:837","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"anonymous reviewer","meaning":"محكم مجهول","example":"An anonymous reviewer suggested","number":838,"id":"b2:838","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"independent","meaning":"تكرار مستقل للتجربة","example":"The published research methodology had not been described clearly enough for an independent replication, and several graphs suggested selective reporting.","number":839,"id":"b2:839","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"transparent methods","meaning":"طرق شفافة","example":"The team examined transparent methods.","number":840,"id":"b2:840","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"scientific credibility","meaning":"مصداقية علمية","example":"Scientific credibility depends on being willing to question a favourite idea and publicly acknowledge when the evidence no longer supports it.","number":841,"id":"b2:841","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"publish or perish","meaning":"انشر أو اندثر","example":"Conflict disclosure and the pressure of publish or perish.","number":842,"id":"b2:842","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"professional","meaning":"عواقب مهنية","example":"They also discussed professional consequences and academic reputation.","number":843,"id":"b2:843","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"ethical investigation","meaning":"تحقيق أخلاقي","example":"An ethical investigation eventually showed that the author had omitted negative results and failed to correct the record after discovering the problem.","number":844,"id":"b2:844","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"correct the record","meaning":"يصحح السجل","example":"An ethical investigation eventually showed that the author had omitted negative results and failed to correct the record after discovering the problem.","number":845,"id":"b2:845","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"retract a paper","meaning":"يسحب بحثا منشورا","example":"The journal decided to retract a paper while the researchers repeated the work.","number":846,"id":"b2:846","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"genuine mistake","meaning":"خطأ حقيقي","example":"An anonymous reviewer suggested that a genuine mistake might explain the errors.","number":847,"id":"b2:847","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"evidence review","meaning":"مراجعة أدلة","example":"She asked her research supervisor to organise an evidence review before making public claims.","number":848,"id":"b2:848","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"academic honesty","meaning":"أمانة أكاديمية","example":"Maya learned that academic honesty is more important than a dramatic headline.","number":849,"id":"b2:849","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"},{"term":"restore credibility","meaning":"يستعيد المصداقية","example":"But an honest explanation helped restore credibility over time.","number":850,"id":"b2:850","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-34"}],"story":{"title":"The Research Integrity Case","paragraphs":["A celebrated scientist published a study claiming an extraordinary discovery. During peer review of a follow-up paper, graduate student Maya noticed a flawed experiment. The published research methodology had not been described clearly enough for an independent replication, and several graphs suggested selective reporting.","Some colleagues suspected data manipulation and an academic misconduct scandal. Others warned against a plagiarism accusation without proof. Maya understood that statistical significance depends on appropriate methods and a reproducible result. She asked her research supervisor to organise an evidence review before making public claims.","An anonymous reviewer suggested that a genuine mistake might explain the errors. The team examined transparent methods, conflict disclosure and the pressure of publish or perish. They also discussed professional consequences and academic reputation. An ethical investigation eventually showed that the author had omitted negative results and failed to correct the record after discovering the problem.","The journal decided to retract a paper while the researchers repeated the work. The scientist's credibility suffered, but an honest explanation helped restore credibility over time. Maya learned that academic honesty is more important than a dramatic headline. Scientific credibility depends on being willing to question a favourite idea and publicly acknowledge when the evidence no longer supports it."],"questions":["What first made Maya question the study?","Why did she request an evidence review?","What eventually justified retracting the paper?","What is the story’s message about scientific credibility?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-35","title":"The Peace Negotiation","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 35","level":"B2","set":35,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"peace talks","meaning":"محادثات سلام","example":"Two communities began peace talks after years of mistrust over a territorial dispute.","number":851,"id":"b2:851","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"diplomatic","meaning":"انفراجة دبلوماسية","example":"The neutral organiser hoped an international mediation team could achieve a diplomatic breakthrough.","number":852,"id":"b2:852","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"mutual concessions","meaning":"تنازلات متبادلة","example":"A lasting ceasefire seemed impossible because nobody wanted to offer mutual concessions.","number":853,"id":"b2:853","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"territorial dispute","meaning":"نزاع إقليمي","example":"Two communities began peace talks after years of mistrust over a territorial dispute.","number":854,"id":"b2:854","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"lasting ceasefire","meaning":"وقف إطلاق نار دائم","example":"A lasting ceasefire seemed impossible because nobody wanted to offer mutual concessions.","number":855,"id":"b2:855","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"negotiating position","meaning":"موقف تفاوضي","example":"Each side entered the meeting with opposing demands and a different negotiating position.","number":856,"id":"b2:856","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"opposing demands","meaning":"مطالب متعارضة","example":"Each side entered the meeting with opposing demands and a different negotiating position.","number":857,"id":"b2:857","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"political legitimacy","meaning":"شرعية سياسية","example":"At first, leaders argued about political legitimacy and the need for a security guarantee.","number":858,"id":"b2:858","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"security guarantee","meaning":"ضمان أمني","example":"At first, leaders argued about political legitimacy and the need for a security guarantee.","number":859,"id":"b2:859","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"international","meaning":"وساطة دولية","example":"The neutral organiser hoped an international mediation team could achieve a diplomatic breakthrough.","number":860,"id":"b2:860","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"civil society","meaning":"مجتمع مدني","example":"However, civil society groups had already created a grassroots initiative to repair shared schools and markets.","number":861,"id":"b2:861","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"grassroots initiative","meaning":"مبادرة شعبية","example":"However, civil society groups had already created a grassroots initiative to repair shared schools and markets.","number":862,"id":"b2:862","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"mistrust","meaning":"انعدام الثقة","example":"Two communities began peace talks after years of mistrust over a territorial dispute.","number":863,"id":"b2:863","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"confidence-building","meaning":"إجراء لبناء الثقة","example":"The mediator proposed a confidence-building measure.","number":864,"id":"b2:864","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"compromise proposal","meaning":"مقترح تسوية","example":"Both sides considered a compromise proposal.","number":865,"id":"b2:865","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"constructive","meaning":"حوار بناء","example":"Through constructive dialogue and strategic patience.","number":866,"id":"b2:866","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"formal ratification","meaning":"تصديق رسمي","example":"Formal ratification required time.","number":867,"id":"b2:867","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"potential obstacle","meaning":"عائق محتمل","example":"And any potential obstacle could still damage the fragile agreement.","number":868,"id":"b2:868","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"responsible","meaning":"قيادة مسؤولة","example":"Responsible leadership eventually brought the parties closer to a shared future.","number":869,"id":"b2:869","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"strategic patience","meaning":"صبر استراتيجي","example":"Through constructive dialogue and strategic patience.","number":870,"id":"b2:870","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"peaceful coexistence","meaning":"تعايش سلمي","example":"Their work showed that peaceful coexistence was possible even before every political question was settled.","number":871,"id":"b2:871","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"shared future","meaning":"مستقبل مشترك","example":"Responsible leadership eventually brought the parties closer to a shared future.","number":872,"id":"b2:872","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"monitor","meaning":"يراقب التنفيذ","example":"The mediator proposed a confidence-building measure: representatives would meet regularly and allow observers to monitor implementation of small agreements.","number":873,"id":"b2:873","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"fragile agreement","meaning":"اتفاق هش","example":"And any potential obstacle could still damage the fragile agreement.","number":874,"id":"b2:874","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"},{"term":"historic","meaning":"انفراجة تاريخية","example":"The meeting ended with a historic breakthrough.","number":875,"id":"b2:875","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-35"}],"story":{"title":"The Peace Negotiation","paragraphs":["Two communities began peace talks after years of mistrust over a territorial dispute. Each side entered the meeting with opposing demands and a different negotiating position. The neutral organiser hoped an international mediation team could achieve a diplomatic breakthrough.","At first, leaders argued about political legitimacy and the need for a security guarantee. A lasting ceasefire seemed impossible because nobody wanted to offer mutual concessions. However, civil society groups had already created a grassroots initiative to repair shared schools and markets. Their work showed that peaceful coexistence was possible even before every political question was settled.","The mediator proposed a confidence-building measure: representatives would meet regularly and allow observers to monitor implementation of small agreements. Through constructive dialogue and strategic patience, both sides considered a compromise proposal. Formal ratification required time, and any potential obstacle could still damage the fragile agreement.","Responsible leadership eventually brought the parties closer to a shared future. The meeting ended with a historic breakthrough, but the mediator refused to declare every problem solved. Real peace, she said, needs everyday cooperation and accountable follow-through. The students who watched the talks learned that a promise made in public is only the beginning of trust, not the end of disagreement."],"questions":["Why did the talks initially stall?","What role did local civil society play?","Why did the mediator focus on small monitored steps?","Why was the breakthrough not described as final peace?"]}},{"id":"b2-set-36","title":"The Final B2 Puzzle","subtitle":"B2 reading adventure 36","level":"B2","set":36,"emoji":"🌊","color":"#9278F7","words":[{"term":"intellectual curiosity","meaning":"فضول فكري","example":"We needed intellectual curiosity.","number":876,"id":"b2:876","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"nuanced argument","meaning":"حجة دقيقة ومتوازنة","example":"Independent judgement and a nuanced argument rather than a quick guess.","number":877,"id":"b2:877","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"independent","meaning":"حكم مستقل","example":"Independent judgement and a nuanced argument rather than a quick guess.","number":878,"id":"b2:878","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"critical evaluation","meaning":"تقييم نقدي","example":"Sara began with critical evaluation.","number":879,"id":"b2:879","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"interpret evidence","meaning":"يفسر الأدلة","example":"The first instruction was to interpret evidence and distinguish fact from opinion.","number":880,"id":"b2:880","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"challenge","meaning":"يتحدى الافتراضات","example":"Leo tried to challenge assumptions while Amira reminded everyone to weigh alternatives.","number":881,"id":"b2:881","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"weigh alternatives","meaning":"يوازن البدائل","example":"Leo tried to challenge assumptions while Amira reminded everyone to weigh alternatives.","number":882,"id":"b2:882","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"distinguish fact from","meaning":"يميز الحقيقة من الرأي","example":"The first instruction was to interpret evidence and distinguish fact from opinion.","number":883,"id":"b2:883","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"counterargument","meaning":"حجة مضادة","example":"Each member offered a counterargument and searched for a coherent explanation.","number":884,"id":"b2:884","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"coherent explanation","meaning":"تفسير مترابط","example":"Each member offered a counterargument and searched for a coherent explanation.","number":885,"id":"b2:885","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"balanced conclusion","meaning":"خلاصة متوازنة","example":"Constructive criticism and a balanced conclusion.","number":886,"id":"b2:886","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"persuasive reasoning","meaning":"استدلال مقنع","example":"The teacher asked for persuasive reasoning.","number":887,"id":"b2:887","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"ethical reflection","meaning":"تأمل أخلاقي","example":"The most difficult clue required ethical reflection.","number":888,"id":"b2:888","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"cross-disciplinary","meaning":"تفكير عابر للتخصصات","example":"Through cross-disciplinary thinking, we combined knowledge of science, history and society.","number":889,"id":"b2:889","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"collaborative","meaning":"حل مشكلات تعاوني","example":"Our collaborative problem-solving turned into an evidence-based decision after thoughtful leadership encouraged everyone to speak.","number":890,"id":"b2:890","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"evidence-based","meaning":"قرار مبني على الأدلة","example":"Our collaborative problem-solving turned into an evidence-based decision after thoughtful leadership encouraged everyone to speak.","number":891,"id":"b2:891","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"long-term","meaning":"نتيجة بعيدة المدى","example":"A choice that seemed efficient carried a long-term consequence for another group.","number":892,"id":"b2:892","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"tolerate uncertainty","meaning":"يتقبل عدم اليقين","example":"We had to tolerate uncertainty and practise intellectual humility.","number":893,"id":"b2:893","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"intellectual humility","meaning":"تواضع فكري","example":"We had to tolerate uncertainty and practise intellectual humility.","number":894,"id":"b2:894","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"thoughtful","meaning":"قيادة متبصرة","example":"Our collaborative problem-solving turned into an evidence-based decision after thoughtful leadership encouraged everyone to speak.","number":895,"id":"b2:895","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"constructive criticism","meaning":"نقد بناء","example":"Constructive criticism and a balanced conclusion.","number":896,"id":"b2:896","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"adapt one's","meaning":"يعدل وجهة نظره","example":"We used deliberate practice to improve our explanation and learned to adapt one's viewpoint when stronger information appeared.","number":897,"id":"b2:897","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"deliberate practice","meaning":"تدريب مقصود","example":"We used deliberate practice to improve our explanation and learned to adapt one's viewpoint when stronger information appeared.","number":898,"id":"b2:898","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"deeper","meaning":"فهم أعمق","example":"The message inside celebrated deeper understanding.","number":899,"id":"b2:899","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"},{"term":"lifelong quest","meaning":"رحلة تعلم دائمة","example":"We realised that every challenge in the book had prepared us for a lifelong quest: learning to think carefully, listen honestly and reconsider even the ideas we once held with confidence.","number":900,"id":"b2:900","level":"B2","lessonId":"b2-set-36"}],"story":{"title":"The Final B2 Puzzle","paragraphs":["In the final room of the Vocabulary Quest, our team faced a puzzle with several convincing answers. We needed intellectual curiosity, independent judgement and a nuanced argument rather than a quick guess. The first instruction was to interpret evidence and distinguish fact from opinion.","Sara began with critical evaluation. Leo tried to challenge assumptions while Amira reminded everyone to weigh alternatives. Each member offered a counterargument and searched for a coherent explanation. Through cross-disciplinary thinking, we combined knowledge of science, history and society.","The most difficult clue required ethical reflection. A choice that seemed efficient carried a long-term consequence for another group. We had to tolerate uncertainty and practise intellectual humility, acknowledging what we did not know. Our collaborative problem-solving turned into an evidence-based decision after thoughtful leadership encouraged everyone to speak.","The teacher asked for persuasive reasoning, constructive criticism and a balanced conclusion. We used deliberate practice to improve our explanation and learned to adapt one's viewpoint when stronger information appeared. At last the final door opened. The message inside celebrated deeper understanding, not simply a correct answer. We realised that every challenge in the book had prepared us for a lifelong quest: learning to think carefully, listen honestly and reconsider even the ideas we once held with confidence."],"questions":["Why could the team not solve the puzzle with a quick guess?","What made the ethical clue difficult?","How did the team respond to uncertainty?","What does the final message say learning is really about?"]}}]);
